INFO 09-15 16:07:45 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-8f18f572f22e4a999817d62dd0783126-0: prompt: 'In the late 18th century, the Italian scientist Alessandro Volta invented the first true battery, known as the voltaic pile. The voltaic pile consisted of alternating disks of copper and zinc, separated by pieces of cardboard soaked in brine. When the two metals were connected by a wire, a chemical reaction occurred, generating a flow of electricity. This invention marked the beginning of the modern age of electricity, and it had a profound impact on the development of technology.\n\nThe voltaic pile was soon improved upon by other scientists, and new types of batteries were invented. In the early 19th century, the British scientist John Frederic Daniell developed a battery that used a copper sulfate solution and a zinc electrode, which was more reliable and efficient than the voltaic pile. This battery was widely used in telegraph systems and other early electrical applications.\n\nThroughout the 19th and early 20th centuries, batteries continued to improve, and new applications for them were discovered. The introduction of the lead-acid battery in the mid-19th century made possible the development of the first electric vehicles, and by the early 20th century, electric cars, buses, and even taxis were common in many cities.\n\nDuring World War II, batteries played a crucial role in military technology. Portable batteries powered radios, flashlights, and other equipment used by soldiers in the field, while larger batteries powered radar systems, submarines, and other advanced weapons.\n\nIn the post-war period, batteries continued to evolve, and new types of batteries were developed. The invention of the nickel-cadmium battery in the 1950s revolutionized portable electronics, making possible the development of portable radios, tape recorders, and eventually, the first handheld calculators.\n\nIn the 1970s and 1980s, advances in battery technology made possible the development of the first laptop computers and mobile phones. These devices would not have been possible without the development of small, lightweight batteries with high energy densities.\n\nToday, batteries are an essential component of many modern devices, including electric vehicles, smartphones, laptops, and renewable energy systems. As the world continues to transition to a more sustainable energy system, batteries will play an even more important role, enabling the widespread adoption of renewable energy sources like solar and wind power.\n\nThe evolution of battery technology has been a key driver of human progress, enabling the development of new technologies and improving the quality of life for people around the world. As we look to the future, it is clear that batteries will continue to be a vital part of our lives, powering the devices and technologies that make modern life possible.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=23, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 902, 506, 5226, 236743, 236770, 236828, 594, 7691, 236764, 506, 12896, 30892, 101030, 155274, 42148, 506, 1171, 1847, 10055, 236764, 3224, 618, 506, 29675, 525, 26106, 236761, 669, 29675, 525, 26106, 31590, 529, 46741, 50536, 529, 14561, 532, 26862, 236764, 15914, 684, 9097, 529, 41670, 70811, 528, 92542, 236761, 3026, 506, 1156, 17257, 964, 6638, 684, 496, 8733, 236764, 496, 7395, 6608, 10997, 236764, 20150, 496, 2727, 529, 14855, 236761, 1174, 17410, 11373, 506, 6534, 529, 506, 4532, 3911, 529, 14855, 236764, 532, 625, 1053, 496, 27725, 4100, 580, 506, 2913, 529, 4181, 236761, 108, 818, 29675, 525, 26106, 691, 4