 19%|█▉        | 192/1000 [00:58<05:57,  2.26it/s]INFO 09-15 16:07:54 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-4ce4ffdc07e64dd3b98cc25d0ceadb1b-0: prompt: 'Sure, here are a few more types of transitional words with their definitions and example sentences:\n\n| # | Type of Transition | Definition | Example Sentence |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 7 | Clarification | Used to clarify or provide additional information | In other words, we need to create a more user-friendly website. |\n|  |  |  | To put it another way, the report suggests that we need to focus on customer satisfaction. |\n|  |  |  | To be more specific, we need to target our marketing efforts towards a younger demographic. |\n|  |  |  | That is, we need to provide more training to our employees to improve their skills. |\n| 8 | Consequence/Result | Used to show a consequence or result of an action or situation | Accordingly, we need to take action to address the issue. |\n|  |  |  | Hence, we need to implement these changes to improve our results. |\n|  |  |  | In effect, our profits have doubled since we implemented the new marketing strategy. |\n|  |  |  | The net result of these changes is a more efficient and profitable business. |\n| 9 | Example | Used to provide an example or illustrate a point | For instance, we can look at how our competitors are handling the same issue. |\n|  |  |  | To give an example, the new software has improved our productivity by 50%. |\n|  |  |  | As an illustration, we can look at how the new product has increased our customer satisfaction ratings. |\n|  |  |  | A case in point is how the new sales strategy has increased our revenue by 20%. |\n| 10 | Purpose | Used to show the purpose or intention of an action or statement | With this in mind, we need to focus on improving our customer service. |\n|  |  |  | To this end, we have developed a new training program for our employees. |\n|  |  |  | In order to achieve our goals, we need to work together as a team. |\n|  |  |  | 