INFO 09-15 16:08:01 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-7985d0fcdfc54a5aab07b1d4e2c92d79-0: prompt: 'The error you are experiencing is likely due to the fact that the `MyMLAlgorithm` class has not been defined. Here is an example of how you could implement this class:\n```\nclass MyMLAlgorithm:\n    def __init__(self, custom_optimizer):\n        self.custom_optimizer = custom_optimizer\n        self.weights = None\n        \n    def fit(self, X, y):\n        # Initialize the weights to random values\n        self.weights = np.random.rand(X.shape[1])\n        \n        # Optimize the weights using the custom optimizer\n        self.weights = self.custom_optimizer.optimize(self.weights, X, y)\n        \n    def predict(self, X):\n        # Make predictions using the optimized weights\n        predictions = np.dot(X, self.weights)\n        return predictions\n```\nWith this implementation, you should be able to use the `MyMLAlgorithm` class as follows:\n```\n# Create an instance of the custom optimizer\ncustom_optimizer = MyCustomOptimizer()\n\n# Create an instance of the algorithm, using the custom optimizer\nalgorithm = MyMLAlgorithm(custom_optimizer=custom_optimizer)\n\n# Fit the algorithm to the training data\nalgorithm.fit(X_train, y_train)\n\n# Use the algorithm to make predictions on the test set\npredictions = algorithm.predict(X_test)\n\n# Compute the mean squared error\nmse = np.mean((predictions - y_test) ** 2)\n\n# Print the mean squared error\nprint(mse)\n```\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any questions.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=7, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None)