 23%|██▎       | 228/1000 [01:06<03:14,  3.98it/s]INFO 09-15 16:08:02 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-1545bb9c9968429a86a69a817e79b568-0: prompt: "NextAuth is a popular library for implementing user authentication and authorization in Next.js applications. Here is an example of how you could use NextAuth to control access to resources in your quiz website builder:\n\n1. Install NextAuth and its dependencies:\n```\nnpm install next-auth @nextauth/client @nextauth/providers\n```\n1. Set up your authentication providers: NextAuth supports a variety of authentication providers, such as Google, Facebook, and email/password. Follow the NextAuth documentation to set up the authentication providers you want to use.\n2. Set up your database: NextAuth requires a database to store user accounts and sessions. You can use a library like `pg` to connect to a PostgreSQL database from your Next.js application.\n3. Add the NextAuth middleware to your server: In your server.ts file, you can use the `nextAuthMiddleware` function provided by NextAuth to add middleware that will handle the authentication process.\n4. Protect routes or resources: You can use the `withAuth` higher-order component (HOC) provided by NextAuth to protect routes or resources from unauthorized access. For example, you could wrap your `/admin` route in the `withAuth` HOC to ensure that only authenticated admin users can access it:\n```\nimport { withAuth } from '@nextauth/client'\n\nexport const config = {\n  auth: {\n    strategies: ['google']\n  }\n}\n\nconst AdminPage = () => {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Admin Page</h1>\n      {/* Add and edit questions form goes here */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\nexport default withAuth(AdminPage)\n```\nOverall, using NextAuth to control access to resources in your quiz website builder is a straightforward process that involves setting up your authentication providers, adding the NextAuth middleware to your server, and using the `withAuth` HOC to protect routes or resources. You can refer to the NextAuth documentation for more detailed instructions and examples.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=24, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 9272, 11610, 563, 496, 4913, 9427, 573, 22743, 2430, 31324, 532, 36605, 528, 12067, 236761, 2092, 6182, 236761, 5715, 563, 614, 2591, 529, 1217, 611, 1451, 1161, 12067, 11610, 531, 2256, 2802, 531, 5405, 528, 822, 32611, 4456, 17929, 236787, 108, 236770, 236761, 18471, 12067, 11610, 532, 1061, 29176, 236787, 107, 2717, 107, 22934, 4476, 2148, 236772, 9343, 1392, 4874, 9343, 236786, 5586, 1392, 4874, 9343, 236786, 69307, 107, 2717, 107, 236770, 236761, 5833, 872, 822, 31324, 15063, 236787, 12067, 11610, 12765, 496, 6236, 529, 31324, 15063, 236764, 1288, 618, 6475, 236764, 8221, 236764, 532, 4553, 236786, 8707, 236761, 22177, 506, 12067, 11610, 13049, 531, 1076, 872, 506, 31324, 15063, 611, 1461, 531, 1161, 236761, 107, 236778, 236761, 5833, 872, 822, 7948, 236787, 12067, 11610, 7087, 496, 7948, 531, 4762, 2430, 10789, 532, 14845, 236761, 1599, 740, 1161, 496, 9427, 1133, 2165, 3078, 236929, 531, 3371, 531, 496, 127764, 7948, 699, 822, 12067, 236761, 2092, 3739, 236761, 107, 236800, 236761, 4140, 506, 12067, 11610, 48267, 531, 822, 5941, 236787, 799, 822, 5941, 236761, 1412, 2129, 236764, 611, 740, 1161, 506, 2165, 4874, 11610, 37162, 236929, 1292, 3847, 684, 12067, 11610, 531, 1138, 48267, 600, 795, 6060, 506, 31324, 1657, 236761, 107, 236812, 236761, 53710, 16266, 653, 5405, 236787, 1599, 740, 1161, 506, 2165, 4060, 11610, 236929, 3715, 236772, 2400, 5280, 568, 236814, 4340, 236768, 3847, 684, 12067, 11610,