 24%|██▍       | 238/1000 [01:08<02:30,  5.05it/s]INFO 09-15 16:08:05 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-2965d91134b64130b21001b9a1f9959a-0: prompt: 'The reason for the infinite recursion is due to the bidirectional relationship between `Form` and `FormSection` entities. When you try to serialize the `Form` entity to return it as a response in the `getFormById` method, it tries to serialize the associated `FormSection` objects. When it serializes the `FormSection` objects, it tries to serialize the associated `Form` objects, which then tries to serialize the associated `FormSection` objects again. This creates an infinite loop, which results in a stack overflow error.\n\nOne way to solve this issue is by using a DTO (Data Transfer Object) to return a simplified version of the `Form` entity without the `FormSection` objects. Here\'s an example of how you could create a DTO for `Form`:\n```kotlin\n@Data\npublic class FormDto {\n    private Long id;\n    private String name;\n    private String description;\n    private boolean isFinished;\n    private List<Long> authorizedAccountIds;\n\n    public FormDto(Form form) {\n        this.id = form.getId();\n        this.name = form.getName();\n        this.description = form.getDescription();\n        this.isFinished = form.isFinished();\n        this.authorizedAccountIds = form.getAuthorizedAccounts().stream()\n                .map(Account::getId)\n                .collect(Collectors.toList());\n    }\n}\n```\nIn this DTO, we\'re only including the `id`, `name`, `description`, `isFinished` properties, and a list of `authorizedAccountIds`. We\'re using the `getAuthorizedAccounts` method to get the list of authorized accounts for the `Form` entity and then mapping them to a list of account IDs using the `getId` method.\n\nIn the `FormController`, you can use this DTO to return a simplified version of the `Form` entity:\n```less\n@GetMapping("/{id}")\npublic ResponseEntity<FormDto> getFormById(@PathVariable Long id){\n    Optional<Form> form = formService.getFormById(id);\n    return form.map(value -> ResponseEntity.ok(new FormDto(value)))\n            .orElseGet(() -> ResponseEntity.notFound().build());\n}\n```\nThis way, when the `Form` entity is serialized, it will not include the `FormSection` objects, which will prevent the infinite recursion error.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=25, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 818, 3282, 573, 506, 18304, 74175, 563, 2779, 531, 506, 170731, 4191, 1534, 2165, 3045, 236929, 532, 2165, 3045, 11827, 236929, 20880, 236761, 3026, 611, 2056, 531, 64403, 506, 2165, 3045, 236929, 13186, 531, 994, 625, 618, 496, 3072, 528, 506, 2165, 828, 3045, 4449, 236929, 1996, 236764, 625, 21727, 531, 64403, 506, 5143, 2165, 3045, 11827, 236929, 7751, 236761, 3026, 625, 14722, 5411, 506, 2165, 3045, 11827, 236929, 7751, 236764, 625, 21727, 531, 64403, 506, 5143, 2165, 3045, 236929, 7751, 236764, 837, 1299, 21727, 531, 64403, 506, 5143, 2165, 3045, 11827, 236929, 7751, 1570, 236761, 1174, 14004, 614, 18304, 7350, 236764, 837, 2536, 528, 496, 10166, 22941, 3165, 236761, 108, 4906, 1595, 531, 8974, 672, 4186, 563, 684, 1699, 496, 622, 6257, 568, 2100, 26333, 8196, 236768, 531, 994, 496, 32741, 3567, 529, 506, 2165, 3045, 236929, 13186, 2180, 506, 2165, 3045, 11827, 236929, 7751, 236761, 5715, 236789, 236751, 614, 2591, 529, 1217, 611, 1451, 2619, 496, 622, 6257, 573, 2165, 3045, 75118, 107, 2717, 44933, 107, 236940, 2100, 107, 2153, 1012, 5959, 22122, 642, 107, 140, 7128, 8099, 1846, 236793, 107, 140, 7128, 2552, 1463, 236793, 107, 140, 7128, 2552, 6492, 236793, 107, 140,