 33%|███▎      | 329/1000 [01:39<03:19,  3.36it/s]INFO 09-15 16:08:36 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-35e535dccb894968abee49fec29e060b-0: prompt: "Here's a combined rclone mount command that includes the best options from part 1 and part 2 to stream 4K videos in Plex with a maximum bit rate of 100 Mbps:\n```css\nrclone mount \\\n--allow-other \\\n--buffer-size 1G \\\n--dir-cache-time 1000h \\\n--drive-chunk-size 64M \\\n--log-level INFO \\\n--poll-interval 15s \\\n--timeout 1h \\\n--umask 002 \\\n--vfs-cache-mode full \\\n--vfs-cache-max-age 12h \\\n--vfs-cache-max-size 150G \\\n--vfs-read-chunk-size 128M \\\n--vfs-read-chunk-size-limit 2G \\\n--cache-dir /opt/rclone/cache/gmedia \\\n--log-file /opt/rclone/logs/rclone-mount.log \\\ngdrive: /mnt/gdrive\n```\nHere's what each option does:\n\n* `--allow-other`: Allows other users on the system to access the mounted file system.\n* `--buffer-size 1G`: Sets the buffer size to 1 GB, which is the amount of data that rclone will buffer in memory before sending it to the Plex server.\n* `--dir-cache-time 1000h`: Sets the amount of time that directory and file metadata will be cached to 1000 hours, reducing the number of API calls to Google Drive.\n* `--drive-chunk-size 64M`: Sets the chunk size to 64 MB, which is the size of the file chunks that rclone will download from Google Drive.\n* `--log-level INFO`: Sets the logging level to INFO, which outputs detailed information about rclone's actions.\n* `--poll-interval 15s`: Sets the polling interval to 15 seconds for checking for changes on Google Drive.\n* `--timeout 1h`: Sets the timeout for API requests to Google Drive to 1 hour.\n* `--umask 002`: Sets the default permissions for files and directories to 775.\n* `--vfs-cache-mode full`: Uses the VFS cache in full mode, which caches all data.\n* `--vfs-cache-max-age 12h`: Sets the maximum age of the VFS cache to 12 hours.\n* `--vfs-cache-max-size 150G`: Sets the maximum size of the VFS cache to 150 GB.\n* `--vfs-read-chunk-size 128M`: Sets the read chunk size to 128 MB.\n* `--vfs-read-chunk-size-limit 2G`: Sets the read chunk size limit to 2 GB.\n* `--cache-dir /opt/rclone/cache/gmedia`: Specifies a directory to use for caching data.\n* `--log-file /opt/rclone/logs/rclone-mount.log`: Logs rclone output to `/opt/rclone/logs/rclone-mount.log`.\n\nAs for whether to mount the Google Drive on an HDD or SSD, it depends on your specific setup and needs. An SSD will generally provide faster read/write speeds, which can be beneficial when streaming large files, but may not be necessary depending on the size of the files you are streaming and the other hardware components in your system. If you have enough space on your SSD, it may be beneficial to mount the Google Drive on the SSD for faster performance. However, if you have limited space on your SSD or your files are relatively small, an HDD may suffice. Ultimately, it depends on your specific needs and available hardware.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=40, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 8291, 236789, 236751, 496, 9292, 637, 29837, 4887, 4991, 600, 5132, 506, 1791, 3835, 699, 912, 236743, 236770, 532, 912, 236743, 236778, 531, 6381, 236743, 236812, 236855, 10103, 528, 127610, 607, 496, 5783, 3103, 3136, 529, 236743, 236770, 236771, 236771, 141533, 236787, 107, 2717, 4497, 107, 236750, 29837, 4887, 621, 107, 726, 8021, 236772, 1538, 621, 107, 726, 12672, 236772, 2086, 236743, 236770, 236823, 621, 107, 726, 5098, 236772, 12655, 236772, 2289, 236743, 236770, 236771, 236771, 236771, 236754, 621, 107, 726, 32676, 236772, 40604, 236772, 2086, 2367