 34%|███▍      | 342/1000 [01:42<02:19,  4.72it/s]INFO 09-15 16:08:38 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-556e2132c670423f98c4ccb9e704f6b6-0: prompt: "Certainly, here is a more comprehensive and specific list of article ideas related to resolving building disputes for homeowners in New South Wales:\n\n1. Common Causes of Building Disputes in New South Wales: How to Prevent Them and What to Do if They Occur\n2. Resolving Cost Disputes in Construction Contracts: Strategies for Homeowners in New South Wales\n3. How to Navigate the Building Dispute Resolution Process in New South Wales: A Comprehensive Guide for Homeowners\n4. Understanding Building Dispute Resolution and the Role of the NSW Civil and Administrative Tribunal (NCAT) in New South Wales\n5. Building Defects and Issues: How to Document and Resolve Them in New South Wales\n6. Resolving Payment Disputes in Construction Contracts: A Step-by-Step Guide for Homeowners in New South Wales\n7. Building Dispute Resolution Through Mediation: How It Works and What to Expect in New South Wales\n8. Understanding Your Rights and Obligations in a Building Dispute: A Comprehensive Guide for Homeowners in New South Wales\n9. The Importance of Early Dispute Resolution in Construction Contracts: Tips for Homeowners in New South Wales\n10. Building Dispute Resolution Through Adjudication: A Guide for Homeowners in New South Wales\n11. How to Choose the Right Building Dispute Resolution Service for Your Needs in New South Wales\n12. Building Disputes and the Role of the NSW Building Commissioner in New South Wales\n13. How to Prepare for Building Dispute Resolution: Tips for Homeowners in New South Wales\n14. Resolving Building Disputes Through Litigation: What You Need to Know as a Homeowner in New South Wales\n15. Understanding Building Dispute Resolution and the Role of the Office of Fair Trading in New South Wales\n16. Common Myths and Misconceptions About Building Dispute Resolution in New South Wales\n17. Resolving Safety Concerns in Construction Contracts: A Guide for Homeowners in New South Wales\n18. Building Disputes and the Role of Builders in New South Wales: What Homeowners Should Know\n19. The Benefits of Alternative Dispute Resolution in Construction Contracts: A Guide for Homeowners in New South Wales\n20. Building Dispute Resolution and the Role of Insurance in New South Wales: What Homeowners Should Know\n\nIt's important for homeowners to be aware of their rights and options when it comes to resolving building disputes in New South Wales. Seeking advice and guidance from qualified professionals, such as a construction industry expert or legal counsel, can also be helpful in navigating the complex dispute resolution process.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=7, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 117494, 236764, 1590, 563, 496, 919, 13611, 532, 3530, 1694, 529, 4676, 6549, 4596, 531, 54564, 3788, 42469, 573, 51179, 528, 1799, 4257, 19842, 236787, 108, 236770, 236761, 13752, 91776, 529, 16087, 226256, 528, 1799, 4257, 19842, 236787, 2088, 531, 59804, 74770, 532, 2900, 531, 3574, 768, 2195, 18453, 556, 107, 236778, 236761, 56782, 1965, 11117, 226256, 528, 22039, 85591, 236787, 62382, 573, 6863, 27923, 528, 1799, 4257, 19842, 107, 236800, 236761, 2088, 531, 98480, 506, 16087, 182079, 47278, 12364, 528, 1799, 4257, 19842, 236787, 562, 61774, 15308, 573, 6863, 27923, 107, 236812, 236761, 40411, 16087, 182079, 47278, 532, 506, 29722, 529, 506, 43202, 13979, 532, 42860, 52847, 568, 10284, 1375, 236768, 528, 1799, 4257, 19842, 107, 236810, 236761, 16087, 164034, 532, 43163, 236787, 2088, 