 34%|███▍      | 344/1000 [01:43<02:30,  4.36it/s]INFO 09-15 16:08:39 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-7c97594b443c41fcb6ff1f0b7bb62c68-0: prompt: 'To add a "Run Weekly Allowance" button to the settings page and create allowance events for each category, follow these steps:\n\n1. Add the button to the `app/views/settings/edit.html.erb` file:\n```html\n<!-- ... -->\n\n<%= form_with(url: run_weekly_allowance_settings_path, method: \'post\', local: true) do |form| %>\n  <%= form.submit \'Run Weekly Allowance\' %>\n<% end %>\n\n<!-- ... -->\n```\nThis code adds a new form that submits a POST request to the `run_weekly_allowance` action in the `SettingsController`.\n\n1. Update the `config/routes.rb` file to add the new route:\n```ruby\n# ...\n\nresources :settings, only: [:edit, :update] do\n  post \'run_weekly_allowance\', on: :collection\nend\n\n# ...\n```\nThis code adds a new route for the `run_weekly_allowance` action in the `SettingsController`.\n\n1. Add the `run_weekly_allowance` action to the `SettingsController`:\n```ruby\nclass SettingsController < ApplicationController\n  # ...\n\n  def run_weekly_allowance\n    if allowance_not_given_since_previous_monday?\n      create_allowance_events\n      redirect_to edit_settings_path, notice: \'Weekly allowance has been run successfully.\'\n    else\n      redirect_to edit_settings_path, alert: \'Weekly allowance has already been run since the previous Monday.\'\n    end\n  end\n\n  private\n\n  # ...\n\n  def allowance_not_given_since_previous_monday?\n    previous_monday = Date.today.beginning_of_week - 1.week\n    AllowanceEvent.where(event_type: [\'spending\', \'savings\', \'giving\'])\n                  .where(\'timestamp >= ?\', previous_monday)\n                  .empty?\n  end\n\n  def create_allowance_events\n    weekly_allowance = {\n      spending: AllowanceSetting.find_by(category: \'spending\')&.amount || 0,\n      savings: AllowanceSetting.find_by(category: \'savings\')&.amount || 0,\n      giving: AllowanceSetting.find_by(category: \'giving\')&.amount || 0\n    }\n\n    weekly_allowance.each do |category, amount|\n      AllowanceEvent.create!(\n        event_type: category,\n        amount: amount,\n        timestamp: Time.current\n      )\n    end\n  end\nend\n```\nThis code adds the `run_weekly_allowance` action to the `SettingsController`. This action checks if there have been any allowance events since the previous Monday using the `allowance_not_given_since_previous_monday?` helper method. If no allowance events are found, the action creates allowance events for each category using the `create_allowance_events` helper method and displays a success message. If allowance events have already been run since the previous Monday, it displays an error message.\n\n1. Modify the `AllowanceEvent` model to include a validation for `timestamp`:\n```ruby\nclass AllowanceEvent < ApplicationRecord\n  # ...\n\n  validates :timestamp, presence: true\nend\n```\nThis code adds a validation to the `AllowanceEvent` model to ensure that the `timestamp` attribute is present when creating a new record.\n\nWith these changes, you should have a "Run Weekly Allowance" button on the settings page that checks if there have been any allowance events since the previous Monday and creates allowance events for each category if not.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=21, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2021, 1138, 496, 623, 7306, 40502, 128223, 236775, 4309, 531, 506, 7846, 3104, 532, 2619, 35166, 4749, 573, 1546, 8038, 236764, 1500, 1239, 6555, 236787, 108, 236770, 236761, 4140, 506, 4309, 531,