 38%|███▊      | 385/1000 [01:54<02:12,  4.64it/s]INFO 09-15 16:08:50 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-94f812c3bbd34cf5a63f802447c80622-0: prompt: 'Put this code in a migration class\nval cluster = CouchbaseCluster.create("localhost")\nval bucket = cluster.openBucket("wisk-couchbase-bucket")\n\n// Execute the query to get the unique venue\\_id values\nval query = N1qlQuery.simple("SELECT DISTINCT venue\\_id FROM `wisk-couchbase-bucket`.\\_default.\\_default")\nval result = bucket.query(query)\n\n// Iterate over the results and run an update statement for each venue\\_id\nfor (row in result) {\n val venueId = row.value().getLong("venue\\_id")\n val updateQuery = "UPDATE `wisk-couchbase-bucket`.\\_default.\\_default AS doc " +\n "SET doc.id = CONCAT(\'item\\_variation\\_\', TO\\_STRING(doc.venue\\_id), \'\\_\', TO\\_STRING(doc.data.id)), " +\n " doc.data.item\\_distributor\\_id = doc.data.id " +\n "WHERE venue\\_id = $venueId AND doc.data.item\\_distributor\\_id is missing"\n bucket.query(N1qlQuery.simple(updateQuery))\n}\n\n// Clean up resources\nbucket.close()\ncluster.disconnect()', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=625, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 25240, 672, 3393, 528, 496, 16064, 1012, 107, 1111, 13627, 578, 152651, 5521, 41833, 236761, 3663, 885, 17294, 1373, 107, 1111, 24211, 578, 13627, 236761, 5265, 54164, 885, 236765, 7892, 236772, 122214, 5521, 236772, 36164, 1373, 108, 715, 61622, 506, 7609, 531, 974, 506, 4709, 19573, 19165, 547, 2979, 107, 1111, 7609, 578, 646, 236770, 5069, 7990, 236761, 19751, 885, 12874, 125046, 19573, 19165, 547, 10912, 2165, 236765,