 39%|███▉      | 388/1000 [01:55<01:40,  6.11it/s]INFO 09-15 16:08:51 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-13a5b2790dc34e6fa6dded316a50cdd5-0: prompt: 'There is a strong connection between continuity and differentiability for a function. In fact, if a function is differentiable at a certain point, then it must be continuous at that point as well. However, the converse is not necessarily true; a function can be continuous at a point without being differentiable at that point.\n\nThe reason for this connection is that the definition of the derivative of a function involves a limit. Specifically, the derivative of a function f(x) at a point x=a is defined as the limit of the difference quotient as h approaches zero:\n\nf\'(a) = lim(h → 0) [f(a + h) - f(a)]/h\n\nIf the limit exists, then the function is differentiable at x=a. However, in order for the limit to exist, the function must be "well-behaved" near x=a, meaning that it must be continuous at x=a.\n\nTo see why this is the case, consider the geometric interpretation of the derivative as the slope of the tangent line to the graph of the function. If the function is not continuous at x=a, then the graph has a sharp corner or a vertical asymptote at that point, and so the tangent line is not well-defined.\n\nTherefore, if a function is differentiable at a certain point, it must be continuous at that point as well. However, a function can be continuous at a point without being differentiable at that point. This happens when the function has a sharp corner, a cusp, or a vertical tangent at that point.\n\nIn summary, continuity is a necessary condition for differentiability, but it is not a sufficient condition. A function must be continuous at a point in order for it to be differentiable at that point, but being continuous alone is not enough to guarantee differentiability.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=5, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 3810, 563, 496, 3188, 5603, 1534, 30180, 532, 26827, 2109, 573, 496, 1292, 236761, 799, 1707, 236764, 768, 496, 1292, 563, 76637, 657, 496, 2953, 1523, 236764, 1299, 625, 1921, 577, 8906, 657, 600, 1523, 618, 1388, 236761, 3153, 236764, 506, 61955, 563, 711, 12832, 1847, 236793, 496, 1292, 740, 577, 8906, 657, 496, 1523, 2180, 1646, 76637, 657, 600, 1523, 236761, 108, 818, 3282, 573, 672, 5603, 563, 600, 506, 8514, 529, 506, 17407, 529, 496, 1292, 13842, 496, 4576, 236761, 39799, 236764, 506, 17407, 529, 496, 1292, 517, 236769, 236781, 236768, 657, 496, 1523, 1123, 236784, 236746, 563, 5221, 618, 506, 4576, 529, 506, 4954, 37689, 618, 534, 12668, 5743, 236787, 108, 236760, 36624, 236746, 236768, 578, 2284, 236769, 236754, 16130, 236743, 236771, 236768, 870, 236760, 236769, 236746, 900, 534, 236768, 753, 517, 236769, 236746, 7066, 236786, 236754, 108, 2859, 506, 4576, 7519, 236764, 1299, 506, 1292, 563, 76637, 657, 1123, 236784, 236746, 236761, 3153, 236764, 528, 1900, 573, 506, 4576, 531, 2849, 236764, 506, 1292, 1921, 577, 623, 7368, 236772, 208493, 236775, 3541, 1123, 236784, 236746, 236764, 6590, 600, 625, 1921, 577, 8906, 657, 1123, 236784, 236746, 236761, 108, 2021, 1460, 3217, 672, 563, 506, 1624, 236764, 1966, 506, 16085, 16823, 529, 506, 17407, 618, 506, 17918, 529, 506, 30954, 1757, 531, 506, 3753, 529, 506, 1292, 236761, 1637, 506, 1292, 563, 711, 8906, 657, 1123, 236784, 236746, 236764, 1299, 506, 3753, 815, 496, 14658, 9895, 653, 496, 9351, 211562, 657, 600, 1523, 236764, 532, 834, 506, 30954, 1757, 563, 711, 1388, 236772, 22503, 236761, 108, 20416, 236764, 768, 496, 1292, 563, 76637, 657, 496, 2953, 1523, 236764, 625, 1921, 577, 8906, 