INFO 09-15 16:08:53 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-e8e489ee117f4bdf8f4a552d7f996607-0: prompt: 'To optimize the parameters Kc, Ko, and kN using the optim function, you need to define an objective function that takes these parameters as inputs and returns a value that you want to minimize or maximize. In this case, you could define the objective function to be the sum of squared errors between the calculated denitrification N2O fluxes and the observed denitrification N2O fluxes in the input data. Here\'s an example R code to do this:\n```r\n# Load the required package\nlibrary(readxl)\n\n# Read the input data from the Excel sheet\nInput_Data <- read_excel("C:/Users/tadna/Box/CABBI Post doc/AGRO_IBIS/Flux data/synthetic_data_denitrification.xlsx", sheet = "Input Data")\n\n# Define the function for denitrification\ncalculate_denitrification_n2o_flux <- function(T, W, N, C, O2, kN, Kc, Ko, p = 0.5, Nef = 0.05, N2Of = 0.01) {\n  # Calculate fC\n  fC <- C / (Kc + C)\n  \n  # Calculate fO\n  fO <- 1 / (1 + (Ko / O2)^p)\n  \n  # Calculate the denitrification rate\n  Denitrication_rate <- kN * fC * fO\n  \n  # Calculate the N2O flux\n  Denitrication_N2O_Fluxes <- Denitrication_rate * (1 - Nef) * N2Of\n  \n  # Return the N2O flux\n  return(Denitrication_N2O_Fluxes)\n}\n\n# Define the objective function to minimize the sum of squared errors between the calculated denitrification N2O fluxes and the observed denitrification N2O fluxes\nobjective_function <- function(params) {\n  kN <- params[1]\n  Kc <- params[2]\n  Ko <- params[3]\n  \n  # Calculate the denitrification N2O fluxes using the current parameter values\n  Denitrification_N2O_Fluxes <- apply(Input_Data, 1, function(row) {\n    calculate_denitrification_n2o_flux(row[1], row[2], row[3], row[4], row[5], kN, Kc, Ko)\n  })\n  \n  # Calculate the sum of squared errors between the calculated denitrification N2O fluxes and the observed denitrification N2O fluxes\n  SSE <- sum((Denitrification_N2O_Fluxes - Input_Data$Denitrification_N2O_Fluxes)^2)\n  \n  # Return the sum of squared errors\n  return(SSE)\n}\n\n# Set the initial values of the parameters to optimize\nparams_init <- c(0.004, 15000, 0.084)\n\n# Use the optim function to optimize the parameters\nparams_opt <- optim(params_init, objective_function)$par\n\n# Print the optimized parameters\ncat("Optimized kN =", params_opt[1], "\\n")\ncat("Optimized Kc =", params_opt[2], "\\n")\ncat("Optimized Ko =", params_opt[3], "\\n")\n```\nNote that in the example code above, I assumed that the input data has a column named "Denitrification\\_N2O\\_Fluxes" that contains the observed denitrification N2O fluxes. You may need to modify the code if your input data has a different column name for the observed denitrification N2O fluxes.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=10, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2021, 30726, 506, 6137, 30595, 236764, 16320, 236764, 532, 227019, 1699, 506, 6685, 1292, 236764, 611, 1202, 531, 8540, 614, 12092, 1292, 600, 4716, 1239, 6137, 618, 9103, 532, 7623, 496, 1550, 600, 611, 1461, 531, 24700, 653, 29893, 236761, 799, 672, 1624, 236764, 611, 1451, 8540, 506, 12092, 1292, 531, 577, 506, 2324, 529, 20218, 9825, 1534, 506, 9255, 141551, 646, 236778, 236806, 54007, 532, 506, 5773, 141551, 646, 236778, 236806, 54007, 528, 506, 2744, 1262, 236761, 5715, 236789, 236751, 614, 2591, 630, 3393, 531, 776, 672, 236787, 107, 2717, 236750, 107, 236865, 16959, 506, 3149, 8289, 107, 12195, 236769, 1399, 18765, 236768, 108, 236865, 8847, 506, 2744, 1262, 699, 506, 20824, 10988, 107, 4661, 236779, 2100, 4778, 1676, 236779, 47779, 885,