INFO 09-15 16:09:17 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-048693c6ddd4448897f390e6be02ef2a-0: prompt: "Certainly! Here's an example of how to calculate the intrinsic value of a hypothetical company using a discounted cash flow (DCF) analysis:\n\nAssume that the company is expected to generate $100 million in annual free cash flow for the next 10 years, and that the discount rate (also known as the cost of capital) is 10%.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the present value of each year's free cash flow using the discount rate. To do this, we use the formula:\n\nPV = FCF / (1 + r)^n\n\nwhere PV is the present value, FCF is the free cash flow, r is the discount rate, and n is the number of years in the future.\n\nYear 1: PV = $100 million / (1 + 0.10)^1 = $90.91 million\nYear 2: PV = $100 million / (1 + 0.10)^2 = $82.64 million\nYear 3: PV = $100 million / (1 + 0.10)^3 = $75.13 million\nYear 4: PV = $100 million / (1 + 0.10)^4 = $68.30 million\nYear 5: PV = $100 million / (1 + 0.10)^5 = $62.09 million\nYear 6: PV = $100 million / (1 + 0.10)^6 = $56.38 million\nYear 7: PV = $100 million / (1 + 0.10)^7 = $51.11 million\nYear 8: PV = $100 million / (1 + 0.10)^8 = $46.23 million\nYear 9: PV = $100 million / (1 + 0.10)^9 = $41.70 million\nYear 10: PV = $100 million / (1 + 0.10)^10 = $37.48 million\n\nStep 2: Add up the present values of each year's free cash flow to get the total present value of the company's cash flows. In this example, the total present value is:\n\n$90.91 million + $82.64 million + $75.13 million + $68.30 million + $62.09 million + $56.38 million + $51.11 million + $46.23 million + $41.70 million + $37.48 million = $611.97 million\n\nStep 3: Subtract the company's total debt and any other liabilities to arrive at the company's net present value. For example, if the company has $100 million in debt and $50 million in other liabilities, the net present value would be:\n\n$611.97 million - $150 million = $461.97 million\n\nThis is the estimated intrinsic value of the company based on the assumptions used in the DCF analysis. If the current market price of the company's shares is below this value, it may be considered undervalued and a potential investment opportunity. Of course, investors should always conduct further analysis and due diligence before making any investment decisions.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=8, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 117494, 236888, 5715, 236789, 236751, 614, 2591, 529, 1217, 531, 9279, 506, 35821, 1550, 529, 496, 62954, 2544, 1699, 496, 53838, 8216, 2727, 568, 12622, 236811, 236768, 3671, 236787, 108, 74581, 600, 506, 2544, 563, 4275, 531, 8729, 609, 236770, 236771, 236771, 3625, 528, 7384, 2196, 8216, 2727, 573, 506, 2148, 236743, 236770, 236771, 1518, 236764, 532, 600, 506, 12223, 3136, 568, 23681, 3224, 618, 506, 2157, 529, 5279, 236768, 563, 236743, 236770, 236771, 9525, 108, 5471, 236743, 236770, 236787, 22241, 506, 1861, 1550, 529, 1546, 1051, 236789, 236751, 2196, 8216, 2727, 1699, 506, 12223, 3136, 236761, 2282, 776, 672, 236764, 692, 1161, 506, 6581, 236787, 108, 32185, 578, 633, 13880, 965, 568, 236770, 900, 637, 13365, 236749, 108, 3350, 32985, 563, 506, 1861, 1550, 236764, 633, 13880, 563, 506, 2196, 8216, 2727, 236764, 637, 563, 506, 12223, 3136, 236764, 532, 538, 563, 506, 1548, 529, 1518, 528, 506, 3402, 236761, 108, 16431, 236743, 236770, 236787, 32985, 578, 609, 236770, 236771, 236771, 3625, 965, 568, 236770, 900, 236743, 236771, 236761, 236770, 236771, 13365, 236770, 578, 609, 236819, 236771, 236761, 236819, 236770, 3625, 107, 16431, 236743, 236778, 236787, 32985, 578, 609, 236770, 2