 49%|████▉     | 493/1000 [02:22<01:53,  4.48it/s]INFO 09-15 16:09:18 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-53ad32f0d13241aaa71052159a7335e2-0: prompt: 'Based on the analysis of the "bar.component.html" file, the chart is being rendered within the `<div>` element with the class "bar-chart-container." This `<div>` element is the chart container that we need to reference. Additionally, the button for triggering the download functionality can be placed inside the same component\'s HTML file.\n\nConsidering this structure, here is the updated implementation:\n\n1. Create an Angular directive called `chartDownload.directive.ts` in a shared location (e.g., `src/app/shared/directives/`):\n```typescript\nimport { Directive, ElementRef, Input, HostListener } from \'@angular/core\';\nimport domtoimage from \'dom-to-image\';\nimport jsPDF from \'jspdf\';\n\n@Directive({\n  selector: \'[appChartDownload]\'\n})\nexport class ChartDownloadDirective {\n  // Input property to specify the chart container selector (ID or class)\n  @Input(\'appChartDownload\') chartContainerSelector: string;\n\n  constructor(private el: ElementRef) {}\n\n  @HostListener(\'click\')\n  onClick() {\n    if (!this.chartContainerSelector) {\n      console.error(\'Chart container selector is not specified.\');\n      return;\n    }\n\n    // Get the chart container element using the provided selector\n    const chartContainer = document.querySelector(this.chartContainerSelector);\n\n    if (!chartContainer) {\n      console.error(\'Chart container not found.\');\n      return;\n    }\n\n    // Capture the chart as an image\n    domtoimage.toPng(chartContainer)\n      .then(dataUrl => {\n        // Create a new PDF document\n        const pdf = new jsPDF(\'p\', \'mm\', \'a4\');\n\n        // Add the captured image to the PDF document\n        pdf.addImage(dataUrl, \'PNG\', 15, 15, 180, 180);\n\n        // Save the PDF file\n        pdf.save(\'chart.pdf\');\n      })\n      .catch(error => {\n        console.error(\'Error capturing chart:\', error);\n      });\n  }\n}\n```\n1. Register the directive in the appropriate Angular module (e.g., `src/app/shared/shared.module.ts`).\n2. Use the `[appChartDownload]` directive on any button element in the HTML templates of the dashboard components and specify the chart container selector as an input to the directive:\n```html\n<!-- Example usage of the directive -->\n<div class="bar-chart-container">\n  <!-- D3 chart content -->\n</div>\n\n<!-- Add a button to trigger the download and specify the chart container selector -->\n<button [appChartDownload]="\'.bar-chart-container\'">Download Chart as PDF</button>\n```\nThe `appChartDownload` directive is now configured to accept the chart container selector (class or ID) as an input. In this example, the class "bar-chart-container" is specified as the chart container. The directive listens for click events on the button element, captures the chart within the specified chart container as an image, and generates a PDF file for download.\n\nYou can apply this directive to other chart components by specifying the appropriate chart container selector for each component.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=43, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 22515, 580, 506, 3671, 529, 506, 623, 2230, 236761, 7544, 236761, 3185, 236775, 2129, 236764, 506, 9535, 563, 1646, 23428, 2351, 506, 2165, 224, 236929, 3408, 607, 506, 1012, 623, 2230, 236772, 20297, 236772, 6955, 1781, 1174, 2165, 224, 236929, 3408, 563, 506, 9535, 9714, 600, 692, 1202, 531, 5577, 236761, 18741, 236764, 506, 4309, 573, 74156, 506, 6463, 18544,