INFO 09-15 16:09:19 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-05e7ed009d3044f8b52e8dd2f347db2f-0: prompt: "Page 4:\nAs they journeyed through the dense forest, the siblings encountered a rickety bridge that looked like it would break with every step. Sunny, the eldest, was hesitant to cross, but Gentry and Crabby were eager to keep moving forward.\nIllustration: A picture of the three siblings standing at the edge of the bridge, looking out at the vast forest in front of them.\n\nPage 5:\nGentry and Crabby started to cross the bridge, but it started to sway and creak. Sunny, realizing the danger, called out for her siblings to come back. The three siblings worked together, holding hands, to cross the bridge safely.\nIllustration: A picture of the three siblings holding hands, crossing the bridge together and looking at each other with determination.\n\nPage 6:\nAs they continued through the forest, they found a deep ravine that they needed to cross. Crabby, being the youngest and smallest, was too afraid to jump, but his siblings were there to help.\nIllustration: A picture of the three siblings standing at the edge of the ravine, with Crabby looking up at Sunny and Gentry for support.\n\nPage 7:\nSunny and Gentry, holding hands, helped Crabby jump the gap. The three siblings landed safely on the other side, and hugged each other tightly, grateful for each other's help and love.\nIllustration: A picture of the three siblings hugging each other, with the deep ravine behind them.\n\nPage 8:\nThe siblings continued their journey, facing many more challenges along the way. They navigated a dark cave, where they had to rely on each other's hand-holding to find their way through.\nIllustration: A picture of the three siblings holding hands, walking through the dark cave, with a faint light in the distance.\n\nPage 9:\nAs they made their way through the cave, they encountered a group of angry monkeys who were blocking their path. Gentry, being the bravest, stepped forward to face the monkeys.\nIllustration: A picture of Gentry standing in front of the angry monkeys, with his siblings behind him.\n\nPage 10:\nGentry's bravery impressed the monkeys, and they allowed the siblings to pass. The siblings hugged each other, grateful for the bravery and love of each other.\nIllustration: A picture of the three siblings hugging each other, with the angry monkeys in the background, looking on approvingly.\n\nPage 11-24:\nThe siblings faced many more challenges, but they always found a way to overcome them through love and teamwork. They climbed a tall mountain, crossed a fast-flowing river, and escaped a treacherous landslide. With each obstacle, their love and bond grew stronger.\nIllustration: A series of illustrations showing the siblings working together to solve problems and overcome obstacles, with their love and bond growing stronger with each challenge.\n\nPage 25:\nAs they reached the top of the tall mountain, they finally found the treasure of love that they had been searching for. It was not gold or silver, but the love they had for each other. They hugged each other tightly, grateful for their journey and the love they had discovered.\nIllustration: A picture of the three siblings hugging each other, with a background of the vast, beautiful view from the top of the mountain and a chest overflowing with love instead of gold coins.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=14, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 4163, 236743, 236812, 236787, 107, 2205, 901, 9338, 524, 1343, 506, 19707, 6426, 236764, 506, 36791, 26109, 496, 132819, 2019, 11825, 600, 6976, 11