 52%|█████▏    | 523/1000 [02:29<01:25,  5.56it/s]INFO 09-15 16:09:25 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-6ede7aeb32024c00b1dd0b612ffe2d22-0: prompt: "Biological neurons are the basic building blocks of the nervous system in animals. They are responsible for receiving, processing, and transmitting information. There are several components of a biological neuron that are important for its function.\n\n1. Dendrites: These are the branching extensions of a neuron that receive signals from other neurons. They have a large surface area and are covered in receptors that allow them to detect neurotransmitters, the chemical signals used to communicate between neurons.\n2. Cell body: Also known as the soma, this is the central part of the neuron where the cell's genetic material is located. It contains the nucleus and the other organelles that are necessary for the neuron's survival and function.\n3. Axon: This is the long, thin extension of the neuron that carries signals away from the cell body. It can be up to a meter long in some neurons and is covered in a myelin sheath that helps to insulate and protect the axon.\n4. Terminal buttons: These are the small, bulbous structures located at the end of the axon. They release neurotransmitters into the synapse, the small gap between the terminal button of one neuron and the dendrite of another.\n5. Synapse: This is the small gap between the terminal button of one neuron and the dendrite of another. neurotransmitters are released into the synapse and bind to receptors on the postsynaptic neuron, transmitting the signal.\n\nAn example of how biological neurons work is the transmission of a signal from the eye to the brain. Light enters the eye and activates the receptors in the retina, which sends signals to the neurons in the retina. These signals travel down the dendrites and into the cell body of the neuron, where they are processed. The", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=7, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 180415, 30924, 659, 506, 6079, 3788, 11802, 529, 506, 20100, 1458, 528, 8075, 236761, 2195, 659, 7757, 573, 11985, 236764, 8487, 236764, 532, 72670, 1938, 236761, 2085, 659, 3131, 6237, 529, 496, 15898, 60438, 600, 659, 2132, 573, 1061, 1292, 236761, 108, 236770, 236761, 107449, 31065, 236787, 3143, 659, 506, 62771, 25616, 529, 496, 60438, 600, 5908, 14139, 699, 1032, 30924, 236761, 2195, 735, 496, 2455, 3761, 2433, 532, 659, 7438, 528, 34191, 600, 2174, 1091, 531, 6440, 100461, 156762, 236764, 506, 7395, 14139, 1456, 531, 17730, 1534, 30924, 236761, 107, 236778, 236761, 14104, 2742, 236787, 6542, 3224, 618, 506, 105017, 236764, 672, 563, 506, 6082, 912, 529, 506, 60438, 1298, 506, 2145, 236789, 236751, 14707, 2561, 563, 5628, 236761, 1030, 6097, 506, 31197, 532, 506, 1032, 159757, 600, 659, 4127, 573, 506, 60438, 236789, 236751, 16671, 532, 1292, 236761, 107, 236800, 236761, 32846, 498, 236787, 1174, 563, 506, 1440, 236764, 11202, 9980, 529, 506, 60438, 600, 23076, 14139, 3121, 699, 506, 2145, 2742, 236761, 1030, 740, 577, 872, 531, 496, 19119, 1440, 528, 1070, 30924, 532, 563, 7438, 528, 496, 96904, 86036, 600, 7351, 531, 197784, 532, 3856, 506, 188547, 236761, 107, 236812, 236761, 43687, 16893, 236787, 3143, 659, 506, 1944, 236764, 24699, 806, 9108, 5628, 657, 506, 1345, 529, 506, 188547, 236761, 2195, 5588, 100461, 156762, 1131, 506, 179481, 236764, 506, 1944, 11302, 1534, 506, 12612, 4309, 529, 886, 60438, 532, 506, 55685, 3178, 529, 2264, 236761, 107, 236810, 236761, 25863, 9860, 236787, 1174, 563, 506, 1944, 11302, 1534, 506, 12612, 4309, 529, 886, 60438, 532, 506, 55685, 3178, 529, 2