 56%|█████▌    | 557/1000 [02:37<04:40,  1.58it/s]INFO 09-15 16:09:33 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-d4f77e1644f0412d91a5afc4e06384e7-0: prompt: "Companies are legal entities that are formed for various purposes, including conducting business activities, providing services, or carrying out social welfare activities. Based on their mode of incorporation, ownership, and management, companies can be classified into various types. In this answer, we will discuss the different types of companies.\n\n1. Sole Proprietorship:\n\nA sole proprietorship is a type of business entity where an individual owns and manages the business. This is the simplest form of business entity and requires minimal legal formalities for its formation. The owner is solely responsible for the business's profits, losses, and liabilities.\n\n1. Partnership:\n\nA partnership is a business entity where two or more individuals own and manage the business. The partners share the profits, losses, and liabilities of the business. There are two types of partnership- general partnership and limited partnership. In a general partnership, all partners are equally responsible for the business's liabilities, while in a limited partnership, there are general partners who manage the business and limited partners who only invest money in the business.\n\n1. Limited Liability Company (LLC):\n\nAn LLC is a type of business entity that provides limited liability protection to its owners. The owners are called members, and they are not personally liable for the company's debts and liabilities. An LLC can have one or more members, and its management can be either member-managed or manager-managed.\n\n1. Private Limited Company:\n\nA private limited company is a type of business entity that is owned by a small group of individuals. The number of shareholders in a private limited company is limited, and the shares cannot be publicly traded. The liability of the shareholders is limited to the amount of their investment in the company.\n\n1. Public Limited Company:\n\nA public limited company is a type of business entity where the shares are publicly traded. The ownership of the company is divided among a large number of shareholders, and the liability of the shareholders is limited to the amount of their investment in the company.\n\n1. Non-Profit Company:\n\nA non-profit company is a type of business entity that is formed for social welfare or charitable purposes. The profits generated by the company are reinvested in the company's activities and are not distributed among the members or shareholders.\n\nThese are some of the different types of companies based on their mode of incorporation, ownership, and management.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=9, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 86561, 659, 6369, 20880, 600, 659, 8254, 573, 3572, 8616, 236764, 2440, 25479, 1960, 5085, 236764, 6655, 3019, 236764, 653, 13418, 855, 2777, 21916, 5085, 236761, 18186, 580, 910, 5354, 529, 51898, 236764, 18497, 236764, 532, 3997, 236764, 4699, 740, 577, 21296, 1131, 3572, 4458, 236761, 799, 672, 3890, 236764, 692, 795, 3249, 506, 1607, 4458, 529, 4699, 236761, 108, 236770, 236761, 62795, 195186, 13628, 236787, 108, 236776, 11097, 43073, 13628, 563, 496, 1722, 529, 1960, 13186, 1298, 614, 3141, 30047, 532, 36371, 506, 1960, 236761, 1174, 563, 506, 33055, 1183, 529, 1960, 13186, 532, 7087, 11893, 6369, 172135, 573, 1061, 8304, 236761, 669, 8123, 563, 22525, 7757, 573, 506, 1960, 236789, 236751, 19353, 236764, 14672, 236764, 532, 43935, 236761, 108, 236770, 236761, 45012, 236787, 108, 236776, 11403, 563