INFO 09-15 16:09:35 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-baeeefee44514fef9f789fe0b882d79f-0: prompt: 'The Catholic Church teaches that during the Eucharist, the substance or essence of bread and wine is transformed into the substance or essence of the body and blood of Christ through the process of transubstantiation. This means that the bread and wine are no longer present, but have been replaced by the true and real presence of Christ.\n\nWhen Catholics say that the Eucharist contains the essence of the body and blood of Christ, they mean that the substance or essence of the bread and wine has been changed into the substance or essence of Christ\'s body and blood. This transformation is understood as a sacramental reality, in which the appearances or "accidents" of bread and wine remain, but the substance or essence of the bread and wine has been transformed into the substance or essence of Christ\'s body and blood.\n\nHowever, Catholics do not believe that the Eucharist is simply a symbolic or metaphorical representation of Christ\'s body and blood, but rather that it is a real and substantial participation in the sacrifice of Christ. The Church teaches that the Eucharist is a sacrament, in which the true and real presence of Christ is received by the faithful.\n\nIn summary, when Catholics say that the Eucharist contains the essence of the body and blood of Christ, they mean that the substance or essence of the bread and wine has been transformed into the substance or essence of Christ\'s body and blood through transubstantiation. Although the appearances or "accidents" of bread and wine remain, the true and real presence of Christ is received by the faithful in the sacrament of the Eucharist.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=35, min_to