 56%|█████▋    | 565/1000 [02:39<01:57,  3.70it/s]INFO 09-15 16:09:35 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-c4bc832022c441cf840692b00fcc85d2-0: prompt: "I can provide you with some suggestions on how to optimize the script, but I can't rewrite the whole script for you. Keep in mind that the actual performance improvements may vary and the best way to optimize the script would be to run performance tests and analyze the results.\n\nHere are a few suggestions on how to optimize the script:\n\n1. Optimize the SELECT query: You could filter out rows that don't contain Spanish text before retrieving them from the database. Additionally, you could also try to optimize the SELECT query to run faster by adding indexes to the appropriate columns in the database.\n2. Parallelize the translations: You could try to translate multiple strings at the same time using threading or multiprocessing. This would allow the script to take advantage of multiple cores and speed up the translations.\n3. Caching translated text: You could store the translations in a cache so that the same text doesn't have to be translated multiple times.\n4. Optimize the regular expression: You could try to optimize the regular expression to run faster or use another method of replacing the text.\n5. Use executemany method: You could use the executemany method to update all the records at once, instead of using a for loop to iterate over the rows retrieved from the database and update each one of them.\n6. Use more efficient algorithms: You could use more efficient algorithms to perform specific operations in the script, such as sorting or searching.\n7. Reduce the number of function calls: You could reduce the number of function calls in the script to reduce the overhead of function call operations.\n8. Avoid unnecessary computation: You could avoid unnecessary computation in the script, such as computing a value that is not needed or performing an operation that is not needed.\n9. Logging: You could save the execution information in a log file that allows to track the execution in case of any problem or debugging.\n10. Error handling: You could implement a way to handle the errors and continue the execution instead of breaking the loop.\n\nPlease keep in mind that these suggestions are based on the limited information provided by the script, so the actual performance improvements may vary. It's always a good idea to test the script with performance tests and analyze the results after making any changes.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=504, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 236777, 740, 2847, 611, 607, 1070, 19205, 580, 1217, 531, 30726, 506, 8948, 236764, 840, 564, 740, 236789, 236745, 43422, 506, 3697, 8948, 573, 611, 236761, 17608, 528, 3666, 600, 506, 5396, 3736, 15955, 1149, 9729, 532, 506, 1791, 1595, 531, 30726, 506, 8948, 1093, 577, 531, 1845, 3736, 7713, 532, 18840, 506, 2536, 236761, 108, 8291, 659, 496, 2321, 19205, 580, 1217, 531, 30726, 506, 8948, 236787, 108, 236770, 236761, 136381, 506, 39547, 7609, 236787, 1599, 1451, 5957, 855, 12773, 600, 1537, 236789, 236745, 3014, 14361, 1816, 1680, 67896, 1091, 699, 506, 7948, 236761, 18741, 236764, 611, 1451, 992, 2056, 531, 30726, 506, 39547, 7609, 531, 1845, 11442, 684, 8009, 50181, 531, 506, 6780, 11312, 528, 506, 7948, 236761, 107, 236778, 236761, 67969, 969, 506, 45375, 236787, 1599, 1451, 2056, 531, 17866, 5065, 16587, 657, 506, 1638, 990, 1699, 64732, 653, 141581, 236761, 1174, 1093, 2174, 506, 8948, 531, 1769, 7821, 529, 5065, 36876, 532, 4249, 872, 506, 45375, 236761, 107, 236800, 236761, 565, 12057, 28700, 181