 57%|█████▋    | 567/1000 [02:39<01:45,  4.09it/s]INFO 09-15 16:09:35 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-9c0e0a0533be4c2e9ba7649e4f325475-0: prompt: 'The events of this story with dialogue take place in the timeline of Soul Eater: Death Day, a sequel to the Soul Eater (manga) series where Maka and Soul perished after defeating the Kishin in the Battle of the Moon, thus creating an alternate ending to the original storyline:\n\n"Japanese Prime Minister Yasuo Fukuda and his officials were in complete disbelief as they watched the recent news. While Fukuda was already aware of the collapse of Ukraine after Kiev was devoured by a black sphere, which may have also resulted in the death of some Japanese citizens, this latest turn of events was unexpected. Japan had been relatively stable from supernatural threats, thanks to the efforts of the DWMA\'s East Asia Branch located in Tokyo. Japan had maintained a secret alliance with the DWMA in Death City in Nevada Desert, dating back to the aftermath of World War I. In fact, it was mandatory for the Prime Minister of Japan to be a DWMA graduate until the organization severed ties with Japan during the Second World War, after Japan\'s attack on Pearl Harbor in 1941. The relationship was only re-established following the American involvement in the war to surrender in 1945. They were all in complete disbelief, mainly due to the recent news of the Battle on the Moon where the black sphere had covered the creepy face crescent that had existed for millennia. The aftermath had resulted in the deaths of two young students from the DWMA, Maka Albarn and Soul Evans, who were among the casualties after they defeated the Kishin before he shot at them while being sealed away."\n\n(NOTE: This is mostly focused in Japan\'s perspective.)', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], incl