 62%|██████▏   | 618/1000 [02:58<01:15,  5.03it/s]INFO 09-15 16:09:54 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-6154eabc3435464dba9d9067069d4b92-0: prompt: "Sure, here is an example of a Python function that uses Featuretools to extract features for a child pandas DataFrame based on a parent DataFrame:\n```\nimport featuretools as ft\n\ndef extract_features(parent, child):\n    # Create entityset object\n    es = ft.EntitySet(id='data')\n    \n    # Add parent DataFrame as entity to entityset\n    es.entity_from_dataframe(entity_id='parent', dataframe=parent, index='parent_id')\n    \n    # Add child DataFrame as entity to entityset\n    es.entity_from_dataframe(entity_id='child', dataframe=child, index='child_id')\n    \n    # Define relationship between parent and child entities\n    # (assumes that there is a column named 'parent_id' in the child DataFrame that specifies the parent entity for each child)\n    es.add_relationship(relationship=ft.Relationship(es['parent']['parent_id'], es['child']['parent_id']))\n    \n    # Extract features for child entity\n    feature_matrix, feature_defs = ft.dfs(entityset=es, target_entity='child')\n    \n    return feature_matrix\n\n# Example usage\nparent = pd.read_csv('parent.csv')\nchild = pd.read_csv('child.csv')\nfeatures = extract_features(parent, child)\n```\nThis code defines a function `extract_features` that takes two", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=9, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 49190, 236764, 1590, 563, 614, 2591, 529, 496, 17856, 1292, 600, 6178, 37868, 18220, 531, 8430, 4065, 573, 496, 1919, 24483, 83613, 2721, 580, 4