 64%|██████▍   | 640/1000 [03:02<01:01,  5.81it/s]INFO 09-15 16:09:58 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-9bc30132959f4c24b962f9ff9039d374-0: prompt: 'Sure, here is a concise comparison of Procter & Gamble, Unilever, Henkel, Beiersdorf, Reckitt Benckiser, Colgate-Palmolive, Johnson & Johnson, and Nestle in terms of founding year, revenue, profit, number of employees, and market share:\n\n* P&G was founded in 1837, has a revenue of $67.6 billion, a profit of $9.9 billion, employs over 95,000 people and holds a significant market share in various industries.\n* Unilever was founded in 1929, has a revenue of $52.7 billion, a profit of $6.8 billion, employs over 155,000 people and is a global leader in various markets.\n* Henkel was founded in 1876, has a revenue of $22.1 billion, a profit of $2.3 billion, employs around 53,000 people and has a strong presence in Europe and Asia.\n* Beiersdorf was founded in 1882, has a revenue of $8.9 billion, a profit of $1.0 billion, employs over 17,000 people and is a leading player in skin care industry.\n* Reckitt Benckiser was founded in 1814, has a revenue of $16.5 billion, a profit of $3.3 billion, employs over 37,000 people and has a strong portfolio of household cleaning and health brands.\n* Colgate-Palmolive was founded in 1806, has a revenue of $15.0 billion, a profit of $2.4 billion, employs over 36,000 people and is a leading player in the oral care, personal care and household cleaning markets.\n* Johnson & Johnson was founded in 1886, has a revenue of $82.0 billion, a profit of $13.0 billion, employs over 135,000 people and is a leader in various healthcare and personal care segments.\n* Nestle was founded in 1905, has a revenue of $98.0 billion, a profit of $14.5 billion, employs over 308,000 people and is a global leader in the food and beverage industry.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=