 76%|███████▌  | 757/1000 [03:32<00:38,  6.33it/s]INFO 09-15 16:10:28 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-0981ccd744eb40fd8258e341886216f8-0: prompt: 'Sure, I can add obstacle avoidance feature to the drone code. Here is an updated version of the code:\n```python\n# Import necessary libraries\nimport numpy as np\nimport cv2\nimport time\nimport random\nfrom dronekit import connect, VehicleMode, LocationGlobalRelative, Command, LocationGlobal\nfrom pymavlink import mavutil\n\n# Connect to the drone\nconnection_string = \'udp:127.0.0.1:14550\'\nvehicle = connect(connection_string, wait_ready=True)\n\n# Define the obstacle avoidance function\ndef obstacle_avoidance():\n    # Get the current location of the drone\n    current_location = vehicle.location.global_relative_frame\n    current_latitude = current_location.lat\n    current_longitude = current_location.lon\n    current_altitude = current_location.alt\n\n    # Define the size of the obstacle detection window\n    window_size = 100\n\n    # Get the image from the drone\'s camera\n    image = vehicle.camera.capture()\n\n    # Convert the image to grayscale\n    gray_image = cv2.cvtColor(image, cv2.COLOR_BGR2GRAY)\n\n    # Detect edges in the image using Canny edge detection\n    edges = cv2.Canny(gray_image, 100, 200)\n\n    # Find contours in the image\n    contours, hierarchy = cv2.findContours(edges, cv2.RETR_TREE, cv2.CHAIN_APPROX_SIMPLE)\n\n    # Loop through each contour and check if it intersects with the drone\'s current location\n    for contour in contours:\n        # Get the bounding rectangle of the contour\n        x, y, w, h = cv2.boundingRect(contour)\n\n        # Check if the contour intersects with the drone\'s current location\n        if current_latitude > y and current_latitude < y + h and current_longitude > x and current_longitude < x + w:\n            # Obstacle detected, stop the drone and take evasive action\n            print("Obstacle detected!")\n            vehicle.mode = VehicleMode("BRAKE")\n            time.sleep(5)\n            vehicle.mode = VehicleMode("GUIDED")\n            vehicle.simple_goto(LocationGlobalRelative(current_latitude + random.uniform(-0.0001, 0.0001), current_longitude + random.uniform(-0.0001, 0.0001), current_altitude))\n            break\n\n# Define the drone flight path\nflight_path = [(10.0, 10.0, 10.0), (20.0, 20.0, 10.0), (30.0, 30.0, 10.0), (40.0, 40.0, 10.0)]\n\n# Arm and take off the drone\nvehicle.mode = VehicleMode("GUIDED")\nvehicle.armed = True\nvehicle.simple_takeoff(10)\n\n# Loop through the flight path and navigate the drone\nfor point in flight_path:\n    target_location = LocationGlobalRelative(point[0], point[1], point[2])\n    vehicle.simple_goto(target_location)\n\n    # Check for obstacles every 5 seconds\n    for i in range(10):\n        obstacle_avoidance()\n        time.sleep(0.5)\n\n# Land the drone\nvehicle.mode = VehicleMode("LAND")\n\n# Close the connection to the drone\nvehicle.close()\n```\nIn the updated code, the `obstacle_avoidance()` function uses the drone\'s camera to detect obstacles in its flight path. If an obstacle is detected, the drone stops and takes evasive action to avoid the obstacle. The function is called every 5 seconds during the flight path navigation. The `flight_path` variable defines the waypoints that the drone will navigate to, and the `target_location` variable specifies the next waypoint. The `for` loop in the', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=12, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 49190, 236764, 564, 740, 1138, 33974, 65815, 4926, 531, 506, 19311, 3393, 236761, 5715, 563, 6