INFO 09-15 16:10:40 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-0f8ee373be8744498df4ea2792807297-0: prompt: 'Yes, it is possible to use attention-based networks for generating beats. Attention-based networks are a type of neural network that are designed to focus on specific parts of the input data when processing it, rather than considering the entire input equally. This can be useful when working with sequential data such as music, where different parts of the sequence may be more important for generating the output than others.\n\nOne advantage of using attention-based networks for generating beats is that they can allow the model to selectively focus on specific parts of the input data, which can improve the quality and coherence of the generated output. This can be particularly useful if you have a large dataset of audio samples and want the model to be able to generate output that is similar to specific examples in the dataset.\n\nOne potential disadvantage of using attention-based networks is that they can be more complex to implement and train than some other types of models. Attention mechanisms can add additional computational overhead, and implementing them correctly can require a good understanding of the underlying algorithms and techniques. Additionally, attention-based networks may require more training data and computational resources to achieve good performance, as they have more parameters to optimize.\n\nOverall, the decision of whether to use an attention-based network for generating beats will depend on the specific goals of your model and the available resources. If you have a large dataset of audio samples and want to be able to generate output that is similar to specific examples in the dataset, an attention-based network may be a good choice. However, if you have limited resources or are working with a simpler dataset, other types of models may be more suitable.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=18, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 10784, 236764, 625, 563, 2653, 531, 1161, 5700, 236772, 5140, 12230, 573, 20150, 39161, 236761, 64997, 236772, 5140, 12230, 659, 496, 1722, 529, 22823, 3707, 600, 659, 5402, 531, 3213, 580, 3530, 4688, 529, 506, 2744, 1262, 1056, 8487, 625, 236764, 4319, 1082, 11337, 506, 4251, 2744, 15530, 236761, 1174, 740, 577, 6684, 1056, 2844, 607, 48835, 1262, 1288, 618, 4252, 236764, 1298, 1607, 4688, 529, 506, 7501, 1149, 577, 919, 2132, 573, 20150, 506, 3938, 1082, 3496, 236761, 108, 4906, 7821, 529, 1699, 5700, 236772, 5140, 12230, 573, 20150, 39161, 563, 600, 901, 740, 2174, 506, 2028, 531, 73061, 3213, 580, 3530, 4688, 529, 506, 2744, 1262, 236764, 837, 740, 4006, 506, 3325, 532, 64106, 529, 506, 7835, 3938, 236761, 1174, 740, 577, 6412, 6684, 768, 611, 735, 496, 2455, 15297, 529, 9855, 7365, 532, 1461, 506, 2028, 531, 577, 2735, 531, 8729, 3938, 600, 563, 3361, 531, 3530, 8698, 528, 506, 15297, 236761, 108, 4906, 3435, 44097, 529, 1699, 5700, 236772, 5140, 12230, 563, 600, 901, 740, 577, 919, 3996, 531, 4144, 532, 2519, 1082, 1070, 1032, 4458, 529, 4681, 236761, 64997, 15106, 740, 1138, 4767, 32043, 28962, 236764, 532, 22743, 1091, 15195, 740, 1660, 496, 1535, 6611, 529, 506, 15605, 17927, 532, 8403, 236761, 18741, 236764, 5700, 236772, 5140, 12230, 1149, 1660, 919, 4122, 1262, 532, 32043, 5405, 531, 6350, 1535, 3736, 236764, 618, 901, 735, 919, 6137, 531, 30726, 236761, 108, 33062, 236764, 506, 4893, 529, 3363, 531, 1161, 614, 5700, 236772, 5140, 3707, 573, 20150, 39161, 795, 4911, 580, 506, 3530, 7675, 529, 822, 2028, 532, 506, 2487, 5405, 236761, 1637, 611, 735, 496, 2455, 15297, 529, 9855,