INFO 09-15 16:10:40 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-0ebdacb7a3d74c66a95ea21b6a78159c-0: prompt: ')\n```vbnet\n\nWith the parallel version of the algorithm implemented, you can now run the code using different numbers of threads to see how the performance of the algorithm changes. To do this, simply adjust the `num_threads` parameter when creating the `ParallelRandomSearch` object.\n\nNow you have the complete implementation of the random search algorithm with region narrowing for program distribution among processors and its parallel version. You can use the provided XML input file format to create test cases with different numbers of processors (4, 8, 16) and varying program and exchange data to verify the performance of the algorithm. Remember to meet the requirements specified in the problem statement, such as an average of 8 programs per processor and an average processor load of at least 50%.\n```', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=25, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 236768, 107, 2717, 76575, 2108, 108, 3497, 506, 10616, 3567, 529, 506, 8417, 12845, 236764, 611, 740, 1492, 1845, 506, 3393, 1699, 1607, 4945, 529, 25843, 531, 1460, 1217, 506, 3736, 529, 506, 8417, 3731, 236761, 2282, 776, 672, 236764, 5181, 6253, 506, 2165, 3744, 236779, 42669, 236929, 7689, 1056, 7107, 506, 2165, 22926, 19095, 8980, 236929, 2495, 236761, 108, 6445, 611, 735, 506, 4133, 8688, 529, 506, 4940, 3927, 8417, 607, 4128, 91240, 573, 1948, 5296, 3571, 44505, 532, 1061, 10616, 3567, 236761, 1599, 740, 1161, 506, 3847, 27161, 2744, 2129, 6518, 531, 2619, 1594, 3636, 607, 1607, 4945, 529, 4450