 83%|████████▎ | 831/1000 [03:45<00:30,  5.53it/s]INFO 09-15 16:10:42 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-0c59a7c4f0ae48ea8893bf00d9a314f9-0: prompt: "There are several science fiction vehicles that share similarities with the Fast Heavy Lift Transport (FHLT) described here. Some of these vehicles include:\n\n1. Pelican dropship (Halo series): The Pelican is a versatile troop and vehicle transport used by the United Nations Space Command (UNSC) in the Halo video game series. It is capable of vertical takeoff and landing (VTOL) and can carry various payloads and modules.\n2. UD-4L Cheyenne Dropship (Aliens): The Cheyenne Dropship from the movie Aliens is a versatile spacecraft designed for rapid troop deployment and extraction. It is capable of carrying various payloads, including an M577 Armored Personnel Carrier, and can operate in various environments, including atmospheric and vacuum conditions.\n3. Thunderbird 2 (Thunderbirds): Thunderbird 2 is a VTOL aircraft used by International Rescue in the classic science fiction television series Thunderbirds. It has a modular design, allowing it to carry different payloads and equipment to support various rescue and recovery missions.\n4. Skyranger (XCOM series): The Skyranger is a versatile transport aircraft used by the XCOM organization in the video game series XCOM. It is capable of VTOL and can carry a squad of soldiers and their equipment into various combat situations.\n5. Quinjet (Marvel Comics): The Quinjet is a versatile aircraft used by the Avengers and S.H.I.E.L.D. in the Marvel Comics universe. It has VTOL capabilities and can be adapted for various missions, including troop transport, reconnaissance, and aerial combat.\n\nThese vehicles all share the FHLT's versatility, adaptability, and ability to support various mission types, making them key assets in their respective science fiction universes.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=9, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 3810, 659, 3131, 6647, 25769, 11182, 600, 4024, 39692, 607, 506, 20148, 39591, 79493, 16502, 568, 236811, 17287, 236774, 236768, 4970, 1590, 236761, 4943, 529, 1239, 11182, 3204, 236787, 108, 236770, 236761, 226233, 17221, 1837, 568, 65112, 3605, 1473, 669, 226233, 563, 496, 31587, 101827, 532, 7500, 5203, 1456, 684, 506, 3640, 17041, 13510, 17714, 568, 3743, 7427, 236768, 528, 506, 64642, 2948, 2290, 3605, 236761, 1030, 563, 11844, 529, 9351, 134234, 532, 21838, 568, 49150, 3769, 236768, 532, 740, 6081, 3572, 183591, 532, 19505, 236761, 107, 236778, 236761, 74765, 236772, 236812, 236798, 178273, 122671, 1837, 568, 28444, 832, 1473, 669, 178273, 122671, 1837, 699, 506, 6387, 141078, 563, 496, 31587, 51398, 5402, 573, 7226, 101827, 29436, 532, 23680, 236761, 1030, 563, 11844, 529, 13418, 3572, 183591, 236764, 2440, 614, 587, 236810, 236832, 236832, 6691, 2926, 67388, 72747, 236764, 532, 740, 12833, 528, 3572, 18567, 236764, 2440, 26536, 532, 16954, 3439, 236761, 107, 236800, 236761, 190450, 236743, 236778, 568, 125055, 49212, 1473, 190450, 236743, 236778, 563, 496, 55503, 3769, 13558, 1456, 684, 5785, 52242, 528, 506, 9760, 6647, 25769, 13617, 3605, 40520, 49212, 236761, 1030, 815, 496, 37284, 1702, 236764, 10678, 625, 531, 6081, 1607, 183591, 532, 5842, 531, 1894, 3572, 22661, 532, 10941, 29167, 236761, 107, 236812, 236761, 17488, 131004, 568, 236917, 17081, 3605, 1473, 669, 17488, 131004, 563, 496, 31587, 5203, 13558, 1456, 684, 506, 1684, 17081, 6261, 528, 506, 2948, 2290, 3605, 1684, 17081, 236761, 1030, 563, 11844, 529, 55503, 3769, 532, 740, 6081, 496, 18176, 529, 18187, 532, 910, 5842, 1131, 3572, 17262, 12