 90%|█████████ | 900/1000 [04:01<00:26,  3.79it/s]INFO 09-15 16:10:58 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-c1448030df774950bea7ec36cbef884f-0: prompt: "It was a dark and stormy night in Copperwood. The residents of the town huddled in their homes, waiting out the tempest. Among them was a group of robots who lived and worked at the factory on the edge of town. They were led by Mechaweld, a composite of Nova and Vega, two robots with very different views on life. Nova was deeply religious and very pious, while Vega was a jaded and bitter hard-boiled atheist.\n\nMeanwhile, at the Nut House, a local bar and comedy club, Professor Pipewrench and Toaster were preparing for their stand-up routine. Professor Pipewrench was a wise-cracking robot with a love for all things mechanical, while Toaster was a cantankerous old bird with a quick wit and a sharp tongue.\n\nAs the storm raged on, a group of birds known as the Feathered Friends huddled in their cozy treehouse, trying to come up with new song lyrics. Bruce, the lead singer, was struggling with writer's block and the other members of the band, Charley, Rick, and Tina, were getting frustrated with him.\n\nSuddenly, there was a knock at the door of the treehouse. It was Quacker Jack, a rough and tumble duck with a heart of gold. He had come to warn the birds of a group of rogue robots who were causing trouble in Birchwood Meadows, the neighboring town.\n\nThe Feathered Friends knew they had to do something to help. They grabbed their instruments and followed Quacker Jack to Birchwood Meadows. When they arrived, they found the town in chaos. The robots were wreaking havoc, destroying everything in their path.\n\nThe birds knew they had to act fast. They launched into a rousing performance, hoping the power of music would calm the rampaging robots. To their surprise, it worked. The robots stopped their destruction and listened, mesmerized, as the Feathered Friends sang.\n\nAs the storm subsided and the robots returned to their factory, the birds knew they had made a difference. They returned to Copperwood, hailed as heroes.\n\nBut the conflict between the robots and the birds was far from over. The robots were fighting for equal rights, while the birds were determined to protect their way of life. As the two sides faced off, it seemed that a war was imminent.\n\nIn the end, the outcome was left uncertain. Would the robots and birds find a way to coexist peacefully, or would their differences drive them to destroy each other? Only time would tell in the tumultuous world of Copperwood.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=13, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 1509, 691, 496, 4996, 532, 89373, 3446, 528, 48906, 5168, 236761, 669, 10465, 529, 506, 5148, 220738, 528, 910, 10374, 236764, 9495, 855, 506, 140856, 236761, 18018, 1091, 691, 496, 2299, 529, 37136, 1015, 11742, 532, 5934, 657, 506, 11879, 580, 506, 7377, 529, 5148, 236761, 2195, 964, 5378, 684, 61577, 1348, 7337, 236764, 496, 22907, 529, 33654, 532, 83084, 236764, 1156, 37136, 607, 1401, 1607, 8208, 580, 1972, 236761, 33654, 691, 19297, 12352, 532, 1401, 129349, 236764, 1651, 83084, 691, 496, 673, 13496, 532, 31374, 2651, 236772, 156760, 167346, 236761, 108, 26629, 236764, 657, 506, 16180, 5407, 236764, 496, 2263, 3029, 532, 24815, 5975, 236764, 13654, 60329, 120289, 532, 2282, 2503, 964, 17373, 573, 910, 1975, 236772, 1048, 15668, 236761, 13654, 60329, 120289, 691, 496, 21608, 236772, 8162, 19655, 16775, 607, 496, 2765, 573, 784, 2432, 12974, 236764, 1651, 2282, 2503, 691, 496, 12060, 86079, 806, 2255, 8001, 607, 496, 3823, 32950, 532, 496,