 92%|█████████▏| 918/1000 [04:04<00:09,  8.90it/s]INFO 09-15 16:11:00 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-fa86adccbff9414fbbdf6b0ce4baf616-0: prompt: 'Thank you for providing the schema. Based on the information given, I will assume that the `public.event` table contains the information about the sounds detected by the devices, and the `public.sound` table contains the categories of sounds.\n\nNow, let\'s create a query to get the breakdown of sound categories in the top 90% and the remaining 10% as "other".\n```sql\nWITH sound_counts AS (\n    SELECT\n        s.id,\n        s.name,\n        COUNT(e.id) AS event_count\n    FROM\n        public.sound s\n        LEFT JOIN public.event e ON s.id = e.sound_id\n    GROUP BY\n        s.id,\n        s.name\n),\ntotal_count AS (\n    SELECT\n        SUM(event_count) AS total_event_count\n    FROM\n        sound_counts\n),\ncumulative_counts AS (\n    SELECT\n        id,\n        name,\n        event_count,\n        SUM(event_count) OVER (ORDER BY event_count DESC) AS cumulative_event_count,\n        total_event_count\n    FROM\n        sound_counts, total_count\n),\npercentages AS (\n    SELECT\n        id,\n        name,\n        event_count,\n        cumulative_event_count,\n        total_event_count,\n        (cumulative_event_count::float / total_event_count::float) * 100 AS cumulative_percentage\n    FROM\n        cumulative_counts\n)\n\nSELECT\n    id,\n    name,\n    event_count,\n    cumulative_event_count,\n    total_event_count,\n    cumulative_percentage,\n    CASE\n        WHEN cumulative_percentage <= 90 THEN name\n        ELSE \'other\'\n    END AS category\nFROM\n    percentages;\n```\nThis query calculates the cumulative percentage of each sound category and groups the categories that contribute to more than 90% of the events as the top categories and the remaining categories as "other".', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p