 94%|█████████▎| 937/1000 [04:06<00:10,  6.21it/s]INFO 09-15 16:11:03 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-3e12dbb7682c4e188b007a2d9a4adbc4-0: prompt: 'Ah, I understand now. The tuple you provided describes a context-free grammar, which is a type of formal grammar that is different from a regular grammar.\n\nA context-free grammar consists of four components:\n\n* A set of terminals, which are the basic building blocks of the language, in this case {a, b, c, d}\n* A set of non-terminals, which are used to generate the language, in this case {S, A, B, C, D}\n* A set of production rules, which describe how the non-terminals can be replaced with terminals and other non-terminals to generate strings in the language, in this case:\n\t+ S → A\n\t+ S → B\n\t+ A → aS\n\t+ A → cA\n\t+ B → b\n\t+ B → bB\n\t+ B → CD\n\t+ C → c\n\t+ C →\n\t+ D → d\n\t+ D →\n* A start symbol, which is the non-terminal from which the grammar starts generating the language, in this case S\n\nThis grammar generates a set of string that can be represented by this set of rules, for example:\n\n* S -> A -> aS -> acS -> accS ->', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=65, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 24019, 236764, 564, 3050, 1492, 236761, 669, 33228, 611, 3847, 15517, 496, 4403, 236772, 6796, 40095, 236764, 837, 563, 496, 1722, 529, 10781, 40095, 600, 563, 1607, 699, 496, 4841, 40095, 236761, 108, 236776, 4403, 236772, 6796, 40095, 10594, 529, 2390, 6237, 236787, 108, 236829, 562, 1076, 529, 42310, 236764, 837, 659, 506, 6079, 3788, 11802, 529, 506, 5192, 236764, 528, 672, 1624, 642, 236746, 236764, 518, 236764,