 94%|█████████▍| 942/1000 [04:07<00:09,  6.16it/s]INFO 09-15 16:11:03 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-275ed23fd8254e6d81d61a2139377ea2-0: prompt: "Haruka Nanase was always confident in his abilities as a swimmer. He loved the feeling of being in the water, the rush of adrenaline that came with competition. But as a college swimmer, he was starting to feel the pressure. The top swimmer, Albert, was always one step ahead, and Haruka was struggling to keep up.\n\nRin Matsuoka, Haruka's close friend and fellow swimmer, was also feeling the strain. He was training overseas in Australia, away from the support system he had in Tokyo with Haruka and their friends from the Iwatobi Swim Club. Rin and Haruka had a complicated relationship. They were close friends and rivals, but their unspoken feelings for each other were starting to become clearer.\n\nOne night, after a particularly rough practice, Haruka was walking home when he stumbled upon a young woman singing by the river. Her voice was beautiful, and Haruka was immediately drawn to her. They struck up a conversation, and Haruka found himself opening up to her in a way he never had before. He didn't know her name, but he couldn't stop thinking about her.\n\nAs it turned out, the girl was an inspiring professional mermaid. When she took a trip to Australia for a performance, she reconnected with her childhood best friend Rin Matsuoka. When she returned to Tokyo, she and Haruka ran into each other again, and they finally learned each other's names. Haruka was now conflicted with his growing feelings for the girl, especially since Rin also seemed to be falling for her.\n\nThe three of them became close friends, but the tension between Haruka and Rin was palpable. Both of them were struggling with their feelings for the girl, but neither wanted to admit it. They were also dealing with their own personal demons. Haruka was struggling with his confidence as a swimmer, and Rin was haunted by feelings of guilt over his father's abandoned swimming dreams and the death of his older brother.\n\nAs the three of them grew closer, the girl struggled with finding her own dream and guilt over feeling like she was the cause of her older brother's death years ago. Despite the angst and drama, Haruka and Rin both found themselves falling in love with the girl. They went from strangers to friends to lovers, but the journey was not without its difficulties.\n\nAs they all tried to navigate their feelings and overcome their personal obstacles, they were also preparing for college swimming and World Tournaments. Themes of slowburn romance, Ot3, platonic love, and friendship were intertwined with the drama of competition and personal growth. In the end, they all learned to face their fears and embrace their feelings, creating a love triangle that was filled with both angst and happiness.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=69, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 22945, 14636, 38197, 781, 691, 2462, 12081, 528, 914, 22234, 618, 496, 113872, 236761, 1293, 9312, 506, 8178, 529, 1646, 528, 506, 1813, 236764, 506, 20583, 529, 89724, 600, 3588, 607, 8105, 236761, 2024, 618, 496, 8672, 113872, 236764, 668, 691, 6250, 531, 2597, 506, 4204, 236761, 669, 1903, 113872, 236764, 25694, 236764, 691, 2462, 886, 2918, 7531, 236764, 532, 4969, 14636, 691, 22684, 531, 2514, 872, 236761, 108, 236794, 495, 42621, 236756, 16998, 236764, 4969, 14636, 236789, 236751, 3107, 4389, 532, 12339, 113872, 236764, 691, 992, 8178, 506, 9262, 236761, 1293, 691, 4122, 27307, 528, 8187, 236764, 3121, 699, 506, 1894, 1458, 668, 1053, 528, 21038, 6