 14%|█▎        | 136/1000 [00:18<02:19,  6.19it/s]INFO 09-15 16:12:25 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-09d9f450989b4b77835f66abb3db6e5d-0: prompt: 'There are a number of ways you could make an EDA project that compares consumer sentiment to market performance in the technology sector more interesting and engaging. Here are a few ideas:\n\n1. Incorporate additional data sources: You can add depth and context to your analysis by incorporating additional data sources, such as news articles or company financial data. For example, you could examine how changes in company financial performance or news events might impact consumer sentiment or market performance.\n2. Use advanced statistical or machine learning techniques: You can also make your analysis more interesting by using advanced statistical or machine learning techniques to uncover more complex patterns and relationships in the data. For example, you could use techniques like multivariate regression or feature selection to examine the impact of multiple variables on sentiment or market performance.\n3. Visualize the data in innovative ways: You can also make your analysis more visually appealing and engaging by using innovative visualization techniques, such as interactive plots or dashboards. This can help to highlight key trends and patterns in the data and make your findings more accessible to a broad audience.\n4. Tell a compelling story with your data: Finally, you can make your EDA project more interesting by telling a compelling story with your data. This may involve identifying a clear question or problem that you are trying to solve, and using the data and analysis to provide insights and answer that question. By clearly communicating your findings and the implications of your analysis, you can make your EDA project more engaging and relevant to your audience.\n\nOverall, there are many ways you can make an EDA project that compares consumer sentiment to market performance in the technology sector more interesting and engaging. By incorporating additional data sources, using advanced techniques, visualizing the data effectively, and telling a compelling story with your data, you can create a project that is both informative and engaging.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=75, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 3810, 659, 496, 1548, 529, 4861, 611, 1451, 1386, 614, 190288, 2203, 600, 48068, 11713, 27078, 531, 2436, 3736, 528, 506, 4181, 7095, 919, 6121, 532, 21964, 236761, 5715, 659, 496, 2321, 6549, 236787, 108, 236770, 236761, 61268, 606, 4767, 1262, 7021, 236787, 1599, 740, 1138, 8744, 532, 4403, 531, 822, 3671, 684, 40825, 4767, 1262, 7021, 236764, 1288, 618, 4668, 10308, 653, 2544, 4867, 1262, 236761, 1701, 2591, 236764, 611, 1451, 17318, 1217, 3731, 528, 2544, 4867, 3736, 653, 4668, 4749, 2473, 4100, 11713, 27078, 653, 2436, 3736, 236761, 107, 236778, 236761, 6890, 9691, 18090, 653, 5464, 4735, 8403, 236787, 1599, 740, 992, 1386, 822, 3671, 919, 6121, 684, 1699, 9691, 18090, 653, 5464, 4735, 8403, 531, 53144, 919, 3996, 9935, 532, 9994, 528, 506, 1262, 236761, 1701, 2591, 236764, 611, 1451, 1161, 8403, 1133, 72652, 21055, 653, 4926, 6799, 531, 17318, 506, 4100, 529, 5065, 7016, 580, 27078, 653, 2436, 3736, 236761, 107, 236800, 236761, 197332, 506, 1262, 528, 14549, 4861, 236787, 1599, 740, 992, 1386, 822, 3671, 919, 40878, 35745, 532, 21964, 684, 1699, 14549, 44751, 8403, 236764, 1288, 618, 21931, 23299, 653, 148407, 236761, 1174, 740, 1601, 531, 8357, 2307, 15067, 532, 9935, 528, 506, 1262, 532, 1386, 822, 12396, 919, 15283, 531, 496, 6674, 9998, 236761, 107, 236812