INFO 09-15 16:12:29 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-82db3cbc2702409493e8c29de283a1fa-0: prompt: "I apologize for the confusion. It appears that the `--env-file` flag is not supported by the `docker build` command, as it is intended for use with the `docker run` command instead.\n\nTo pass environment variables from a file while building a Docker image, you can use the `--build-arg` flag with the `docker build` command. Here's an example command to build a Docker image with environment variables defined in an `.env` file:\n```bash\ndocker build --build-arg NODE_ENV=$(cat .env | grep NODE_ENV | cut -d '=' -f2) --build-arg MONGO_URI=$(cat .env | grep MONGO_URI | cut -d '=' -f2) -t my-node-app .\n```\nIn this example, the `--build-arg` flag is used to set the values of the `NODE_ENV` and `MONGO_URI` environment variables, which are read from the `.env` file using the `cat` command and the `grep` and `cut` utilities. The `my-node-app` argument specifies the name of the Docker image you want to build.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=27, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 236777, 57428, 573, 506, 19381, 236761, 1030, 7412, 600, 506, 195800, 7291, 236772, 2164, 236929, 8134, 563, 711, 8008, 684, 506, 2165, 39624, 2016, 236929, 4991, 236764, 618, 625, 563, 10518, 573, 1161, 607, 506, 2165, 39624, 1845, 236929, 4991, 5205, 236761, 108, 2021, 1786, 3453, 7016, 699, 496, 2129, 1651, 3788, 496, 48561, 2471, 236764, 611, 740, 1161, 506, 195800, 4907, 236772, 1187, 236929, 8134, 607, 506, 2165, 39624, 2016, 236929, 4991, 236761, 5715, 236789, 236751, 614, 2591, 4991, 531, 2016, 496, 