 22%|██▏       | 224/1000 [00:34<02:59,  4.31it/s]INFO 09-15 16:12:41 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-06dcf78600cc4f858170f47e9c1c1a1b-0: prompt: 'Write a choose-your-own-adventure game where in each section you describe a scene and offer me three choices, labelled A, B, and C. The setting is England during the Georgian period. There is a ball at a manor house. There have been some mysterious deaths, both upstairs and down, and no one knows who or what caused them. I am a spunky single woman in possession of a provincial accent. I am in want of a brooding single gentleman in possession of a good fortune. I have 100 health points and 0 suitor points. If I am murdered, I lose 100 health points and the story ends. If I make a reluctant connection with a wealthy gentleman, I earn 0-50 suitor points (depending how brooding he is). If I collect 100 suitor points, the story ends, and I win. Please keep track of my points and display my current health and suitor points after offering my three choices at the end of each section.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=164, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 6974, 496, 5347, 236772, 17993, 236772, 931, 236772, 127166, 2290, 1298, 528, 1546, 3336, 611, 9779, 496, 8317, 532, 2729, 786, 1806, 12871, 236764, 54802, 562, 236764, 603, 236764, 532, 565, 236761, 669, 6514, 563, 7591, 1913, 506, 87029, 2846, 236761, 2085, 563, 496, 4299, 657, 496, 92224, 3155, 236761, 2085, 735, 1010, 1070, 34640, 19867, 236764, 1800, 58695, 532, 1679, 236764, 532, 951, 886, 10077, 1015, 653, 1144, 7321, 1091, 236761, 564, 1006, 496, 69597, 4221, 3161, 3875, 528