 24%|██▍       | 243/1000 [00:38<02:29,  5.05it/s]INFO 09-15 16:12:45 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-c92ecd9242164929912131bc040acfc4-0: prompt: 'Apologies for the confusion. In the current implementation, we fetch product information from the `IWarehouse` interface. In this case, you can modify the `SalesController` to accept a product ID and quantity sold in the request, fetch the product information using the `IWarehouse` interface, and then pass the product object to the `HandleSale` method.\n\nFirst, update the `SaleRequest` class in the `SalesController`:\n```csharp\npublic class SaleRequest\n{\n    public int ProductId { get; set; }\n    public int QuantitySold { get; set; }\n}\n```\nNext, update the `PostSale` action method in the `SalesController` to fetch the product information from the `IWarehouse`:\n```csharp\nprivate readonly SalesEventHandler _salesEventHandler;\nprivate readonly IWarehouse _warehouse;\n\npublic SalesController(SalesEventHandler salesEventHandler, IWarehouse warehouse)\n{\n    _salesEventHandler = salesEventHandler;\n    _warehouse = warehouse;\n}\n\n[HttpPost]\npublic IActionResult PostSale([FromBody] SaleRequest request)\n{\n    try\n    {\n        Product product = _warehouse.FetchProduct(request.ProductId);\n        _salesEventHandler.HandleSale(product, request.QuantitySold);\n        return Ok("Sale processed successfully.");\n    }\n    catch (Exception ex)\n    {\n        return BadRequest($"Error processing sale: {ex.Message}");\n    }\n}\n```\nFinally, register the `IWarehouse` implementation in the `Startup.cs`:\n```csharp\npublic void ConfigureServices(IServiceCollection services)\n{\n    services.AddControllers();\n\n    // Register your dependencies here\n    services.AddSingleton<IEmailService, YourEmailServiceImplementation>();\n    services.AddSingleton<IAverageDailySales, ThirtyDaySalesAverage>();\n    services.AddSingleton<IWarehouse, YourWarehouseImplementation>();\n    services.AddSingleton<RestockLevel>();\n    services.AddSingleton<SalesEventHandler>();\n}\n```\nDon\'t forget to replace `YourWarehouseImplementation` with the appropriate warehouse implementation.\n\nNow, when the POS system sends a POST request to the `/api/sales` endpoint with a JSON payload containing the product ID and quantity sold, the web service will fetch the product information from the warehouse, call the `HandleSale` method, and process the sale accordingly.\n\nHere\'s an example of the expected JSON payload:\n```json\n{\n  "productId": 1,\n  "quantitySold": 10\n}\n```', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=38, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 22342, 7378, 573, 506, 19381, 236761, 799, 506, 1873, 8688, 236764, 692, 12270, 1698, 1938, 699, 506, 2165, 236777, 149127, 236929, 7937, 236761, 799, 672, 1624, 236764, 611, 740, 17114, 506, 2165, 27286, 4167, 236929, 531, 4242, 496, 1698, 5853, 532, 10489, 5463, 528, 506, 2864, 236764, 12270, 506, 1698, 1938, 1699, 506, 2165, 236777, 149127, 236929, 7937, 236764, 532, 1299, 1786, 506, 1698, 2495, 531, 506, 2165, 19163, 54747, 236929, 1996, 236761, 108, 7280, 236764, 4610, 506, 2165, 54747, 3932, 236929, 1012, 528, 506, 2165, 27286, 4167, 75118, 107, 2717, 236755, 49553, 107, 2153, 1012, 23387, 3932, 107, 236782, 107, 140, 2153, 801, 7303, 1569, 642, 974, 236793, 1076, 236793, 682, 107, 140, 2153, 801, 52948, 80738, 642, 974, 236793, 1076, 236793, 682, 107, 236783, 107, 2717, 107, 9272, 236764, 4610, 506, 2165, 7118, 54747, 236929, 2970, 1996, 528, 506, 2165, 27286, 4167, 236929, 531, 12270, 506, 1698, 1938, 699, 506, 2165, 236777, 149127, 75118, 107, 2717, 23675