 24%|██▍       | 244/1000 [00:38<02:44,  4.61it/s]INFO 09-15 16:12:46 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-191271bbc3cd4c44b0f4e5de370529fb-0: prompt: 'Here\'s the complete updated script:\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python\n\nimport os\nimport sys\nfrom vyattaconfparser import parse_conf\n\n# Format string for hosts file entry\nhosts_entry_format = "{ip_address}\\t{hostname}\\t#{mac_address}\\n"\n\n# Define the folder containing the EdgeOS configuration file\nconfig_folder = "/nfs/home/config/edgemax"\n\n# Find the newest EdgeOS configuration file in the config folder\nconfig_file = max(\n    [os.path.join(config_folder, f) for f in os.listdir(config_folder) if f.startswith("config.boot")],\n    key=os.path.getctime,\n)\n\n# Parse the EdgeOS configuration file into a dictionary\nwith open(config_file, "r") as f:\n    config = parse_conf(f.read())\n\n# Get the DHCP static mappings from the configuration dictionary\nshared_networks = config.get("service", {}).get("dhcp-server", {}).get("shared-network-name", {})\n\n# If there are no static mappings, exit with a non-zero code\nif not shared_networks:\n    sys.exit(1)\n\n# Generate a hosts file from the static mappings\nhosts_entries = []\nfor shared_network in shared_networks.values():\n    for subnet in shared_network.get("subnet", {}).values():\n        for hostname, static_mapping in subnet.get("static-mapping", {}).items():\n            mac_address = static_mapping.get("mac-address", "")\n            ip_address = static_mapping.get("ip-address", "")\n            if all([ip_address, hostname]):\n                hosts_entry = hosts_entry_format.format(\n                    ip_address=ip_address,\n                    hostname=hostname,\n                    mac_address=mac_address,\n                )\n                hosts_entries.append(hosts_entry)\n\n# Write the hosts file to stdout or to a file if the result is not empty\nif hosts_entries:\n    sys.stdout.writelines(hosts_entries)\nelse:\n    sys.exit(1)\n```\nThis updated script correctly extracts the DHCP static mappings from the EdgeOS configuration file and generates a hosts file from them.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=13, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 8291, 236789, 236751, 506, 4133, 10448, 8948, 236787, 107, 2717, 6719, 107, 38752, 20268, 236786, 6264, 236786, 7291, 23181, 108, 1106, 3252, 107, 1106, 14407, 107, 2543, 14908, 1667, 14814, 236760, 15635, 1419, 11299, 236779, 10331, 108, 236865, 36353, 2483, 573, 20472, 2129, 7234, 107, 65749, 236779, 8482, 236779, 5939, 578, 32928, 760, 236779, 7720, 958, 236745, 236782, 58104, 958, 236745, 58320, 12919, 236779, 7720, 958, 236749, 236775, 108, 236865, 31238, 506, 11709, 7906, 506, 20090, 3354, 9831, 2129, 107, 3762, 236779, 17857, 578, 9560, 236749, 8097, 236786, 8147, 236786, 3762, 236786, 524, 29340, 1124, 236775, 108, 236865, 9100, 506, 29962, 20090, 3354, 9831, 2129, 528, 506, 3957, 11709, 107, 3762, 236779, 2164, 578, 2631, 236769, 107, 140, 236840, 585, 236761, 2337, 236761, 7013, 236769, 3762, 236779, 17857, 236764, 517, 236768, 573, 517, 528, 3252, 236761, 61566, 236769, 3762, 236779, 17857, 236768, 768, 517, 236761, 52740, 885, 3762, 236761, 7641, 115204, 107, 140, 2478, 236784, 585, 236761, 2337, 236761, 828, 91310, 236764, 107, 236768, 108, 236865, 39177, 506, 20090, 3354, 9831, 2129, 1131, 496, 19086, 107, 4060, 1932, 236769, 3762, 236779, 2164, 236764, 623, 236750, 1373, 618, 517, 236787, 107, 140, 3762, 578, 11299, 236779, 10331, 236769, 236760, 236761, 1399, 3507, 108, 236865, 4987, 506, 161415, 2002, 56369, 699, 506, 9831, 19086, 107, 17746, 236779, 95794,