 25%|██▍       | 249/1000 [00:40<04:35,  2.72it/s]INFO 09-15 16:12:48 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-e49fb578e47746718a8e6d8c5208be6e-0: prompt: "As I approached my 25th birthday, I found myself feeling restless and unfulfilled. Despite my love for music and my early success as an artist, I couldn't shake the feeling that something was missing in my life. I had fallen into a routine, working a job that paid the bills but didn't fulfill me creatively or emotionally. I was comfortable, but not truly happy.\n\nAs the day of my birthday approached, I began to reflect on my life and my dreams. I thought about all of the musical opportunities I had let slip by, all of the songs I had never written, all of the moments I had missed because I was too scared to take a risk. I realized that I had reached a crossroads in my life, and I had to make a choice. I could continue down my current path, living a comfortable but unfulfilling life, or I could take a risk and pursue my dreams, no matter what the cost.\n\nIt was a difficult decision, but as I blew out the candles on my birthday cake, I knew what I had to do. I was done living a life that didn't fulfill me. I was done letting my fears hold me back. I was ready to take a risk and pursue my dreams, no matter what it took.\n\nThe first step in my journey was facing my fears head-on. I was scared of the unknown, of failing, of not being good enough. But I knew that I couldn't let those fears hold me back any longer. I took a deep breath and stepped out of my comfort zone, reaching out to musicians and industry professionals who could help me take the next step in my career.\n\nOne of the musicians I reached out to was a seasoned veteran in the industry, someone I had looked up to for years. I was nervous to speak with him, but I knew that if I didn't take this opportunity, I would regret it for the rest of my life. To my surprise, he was more than willing to help me. He listened to my music, offered me advice, and even introduced me to a few people who could help me get my foot in the door.\n\nAnother musician I worked with was a young, up-and-coming artist who was just as passionate about music as I was. We hit it off immediately and started collaborating on a few songs. Our creative energy was electric, and we pushed each other to be better every day. I was amazed at how much my music and my confidence had grown in just a few short months.\n\nDespite the challenges I faced along the way, I never gave up. I continued to write music, perform, and network with other musicians and industry professionals. And before I knew it, I was on my way to becoming the musician I always dreamed of being.\n\nIn the end, I overcame my fears and took control of my life. I am now living the life I always wanted, making music that makes me happy, and inspiring others to do the same. I am Kadence, a musician on a mission, and nothing will stop me from reaching my dreams.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=13, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2205, 564, 28360, 1041, 236743, 236778, 236810, 594, 12089, 236764, 564, 1765, 7564, 8178, 95480, 532, 723, 101476, 236761, 18565, 1041, 2765, 573, 4252, 532, 1041, 3649, 2630, 618, 614, 8325, 236764, 564, 9225, 236789, 236745, 31716, 506, 8178, 600, 2613, 691, 9724, 528, 1041, 1972, 236761, 564, 1053, 22303, 1131, 496, 15668, 236764, 2844, 496, 3195, 600, 6382, 506, 19664, 840, 3782, 236789, 236745, 20159, 786, 101648, 653, 44942, 236761, 564, 691, 9650, 236764, 840, 711, 9995, 5293, 236761, 108, 2205, 506, 1719, 529, 1041, 12089, 28360, 236764, 564, 6074, 531, 7495, 580, 