 35%|███▍      | 346/1000 [00:53<01:01, 10.64it/s]INFO 09-15 16:13:00 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-4af9fe148b2e400a93e03370bc5e4363-0: prompt: "* I want the task status to be visually distinguished on the UI by colors, for example: Not started (gray), In Progress (yellow), In Review (orange), Reviewed (green), and Complete (blue).\n* I want to be able to view a document preview in the Tasks screen, so that I can quickly review the document's content.\n* I want to be able to switch between different classification of documents in a dataset, so that I can work on different types of documents without switching to different tasks.\n* I want to be able to switch between different documents within a task, so that I can review or annotate them without having to go back to the task management screen.\n* I want to be able to track the starting date and due date of each task, so that I can monitor the progress and ensure it is completed on time.\n* I want to be able to receive notifications when a task is completed, so that I can keep track of the status of the tasks and take any necessary actions.\n\nAs a developer:\n\n* I want to create an intuitive and user-friendly interface, that allows users to easily navigate and interact with the data.\n* I want to ensure that the application is responsive and works well on all devices and screen sizes.\n* I want to build the application with robust security features, that prevent unauthorized access to the data.\n* I want to implement features for data management, such as creating and editing datasets, creating tasks, and managing documents within tasks.\n* I want to enable users to interact with the data in an intuitive way, such as being able to filter, sort, and search through datasets, tasks, and documents.\n* I want to use colors to differentiate the task status and to make the interface look more appealing and user-friendly.\n* I want to create a preview of the document within the task management screen, so the users can quickly review the content of the document\n* I want to enable switching between different classifications of documents within a dataset.\n* I want to enable switching between different documents within a task.\n* I want to implement tracking of task start date and due date\n* I want to implement notifications when a task is completed\n\nThese user stories can be grouped into several Epics. For example:\n\n* Epic: Dataset management\n* Epic: Task management\n* Epic: Document review & annotation\n* Epic: Document navigation & preview\n* Epic: User interface and design\n* Epic: Notifications & status tracking\n* Epic: Security\n* Epic: Filtering, sorting and searching\n\nAnd each Epic will be divided into smaller user stories that detail the specific functionality.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=41, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 236829, 564, 1461, 506, 4209, 4981, 531, 577, 40878, 23958, 580, 506, 9711, 684, 7913, 236764, 573, 2591, 236787, 3790, 3931, 568, 16024, 779, 799, 22583, 568, 23861, 779, 799, 9352, 568, 28975, 779, 155126, 568, 10671, 779, 532, 26158, 568, 9503, 769, 107, 236829, 564, 1461, 531, 577, 2735, 531, 1927, 496, 2354, 18201, 528, 506, 86164, 4322, 236764, 834, 600, 564, 740, 6077, 3540, 506, 2354, 236789, 236751, 3004, 236761, 107, 236829, 564, 1461, 531, 577, 2735, 531, 5702, 1534, 1607, 15241, 529, 9413, 528, 496, 15297, 236764, 834, 600, 564, 740, 981, 580, 1607, 4458, 529, 9413, 2180, 26182, 531, 1607, 9395, 236761, 107, 236829, 564, 1461, 531, 577, 2735, 531, 5702, 1534, 1607, 9413, 2351, 496, 4209, 236764, 834, 600, 564, 740, 3540, 653, 17543