 36%|███▌      | 357/1000 [00:55<01:33,  6.91it/s]INFO 09-15 16:13:02 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-5f16f94c70de4610a42dd95b945ca294-0: prompt: 'Sure, here\'s a module outline for "Data Analysis with Pandas":\n\nModule 2: Data Analysis with Pandas\n\n* Introduction:\n\t+ Explanation of what Pandas is and why it is important for data analysis in Python\n\t+ Overview of different types of data commonly used in the banking industry\n\t+ Explanation of how Pandas can help banking professionals to analyze, manipulate, and visualize data efficiently\n* Relevance:\n\t+ Explanation of how data analysis is a crucial part of many banking tasks, such as risk analysis, fraud detection, and customer segmentation\n\t+ Overview of different types of data commonly used in the banking industry, such as transactional data, customer data, and market data\n\t+ Demonstration of how Pandas can be used to read and manipulate large and complex datasets\n* Topics covered:\n\t+ Loading and inspecting data using Pandas\n\t+ Cleaning and preparing data for analysis\n\t+ Filtering and sorting data\n\t+ Aggregating and summarizing data\n\t+ Joining and merging datasets\n\t+ Reshaping and pivoting data\n\t+ Data visualization using Pandas and Matplotlib\n* Practical example:\n\t+ Example code for loading and cleaning transactional data from a CSV file using Pandas\n\t+ Demonstration of how to calculate key metrics, such as transaction volume and average transaction amount, using Pandas\n\t+ Example code for joining transactional data with customer data to create a more comprehensive dataset for analysis\n\t+ Overview of how to use Pandas and Matplotlib to create simple data visualizations, such as histograms and scatter plots, to better understand the data\n\nOverall, this module will provide learners with practical skills for using Pandas to analyze, manipulate, and visualize data in the banking industry. Learners will come away from this module with an understanding of how to read and prepare data for analysis, filter and sort data to extract insights, join and merge datasets to create more comprehensive views of the data, and visualize data to better understand trends and patterns.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=6, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 49190, 236764, 1590, 236789, 236751, 496, 9173, 18161, 573, 623, 2100, 13768, 607, 157202, 1083, 108, 7988, 236743, 236778, 236787, 5774, 13768, 607, 157202, 108, 236829, 23051, 236787, 107, 255968, 236862, 107182, 529, 1144, 157202, 563, 532, 3217, 625, 563, 2132, 573, 1262, 3671, 528, 17856, 107, 255968, 236862, 41959, 529, 1607, 4458, 529, 1262, 14003, 1456, 528, 506, 19257, 3956, 107, 255968, 236862, 107182, 529, 1217, 157202, 740, 1601, 19257, 14477, 531, 18840, 236764, 52266, 236764, 532, 50611, 1262, 23057, 107, 236829, 202571, 236787, 107, 255968, 236862, 107182, 529, 1217, 1262, 3671, 563, 496, 13832, 912, 529, 1551, 19257, 9395, 236764, 1288, 618, 4652, 3671, 236764, 15797, 12692, 236764, 532, 5602, 51761, 107, 255968, 236862, 41959, 529, 1607, 4458, 529, 1262, 14003, 1456, 528, 506, 19257, 3956, 236764, 1288, 618, 129760, 1262, 236764, 5602, 1262, 236764, 532, 2436, 1262, 107, 255968, 236862, 134400, 529, 1217, 157202, 740, 577, 1456, 531, 1676, 532, 52266, 2455, 532, 3996, 32542, 107, 236829, 66864, 7438, 236787, 107, 255968, 236862, 55366, 532, 101882, 1262, 1699, 157202, 107, 255968, 236862, 46749, 532, 17373, 1262, 573, 3671, 107, 255968, 236862, 199692, 532, 37007, 1262, 107, 255968, 236862, 29669, 2291, 1194, 532, 151847, 1262, 107, 255968, 236862, 136291, 532, 66486, 32542, 107, 255968, 2368