INFO 09-15 16:13:02 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-9bbc93bf67d44667a201e9d5ed9597a0-0: prompt: 'Save this description and purposes of the attributes:\nThe PrimaryDrivers table is part of the Vehicle owner and user management service. It is used to store information about the primary driver of a car. The table has the following attributes:\n\nVIN (string): the VIN of the car\nPrimaryDriverID (string): the Polestar ID of the primary driver\nStartTimestamp (number): the timestamp when the primary driver was registered\nEndTimestamp (number): the timestamp when the primary driver was unregistered (if applicable)\nChangeSource (string): the source of the change (either "API" or "Event")\nOrderID (string): the order ID of the event that caused the change (if applicable)\nEventTimestamp (number): the timestamp when the event was emitted (if applicable)\nUserID (string): the user ID of the user that made the update through the API (if applicable)\nClientID (string): the client ID of the service that made the update through the API (if applicable)\nSystem (string): the name of the system that made the update (if applicable)\nIsActive (boolean): a flag indicating whether the primary driver is currently active or not\nPreviousOrderIDs (list): a list of previous order IDs (if applicable)\nThe purpose of each attribute is as follows:\n\nVIN: This attribute is used to identify the car that the primary driver is registered for.\nPrimaryDriverID: This attribute is used to store the Polestar ID of the primary driver.\nStartTimestamp: This attribute is used to store the timestamp when the primary driver was registered.\nEndTimestamp: This attribute is used to store the timestamp when the primary driver was unregistered (if applicable).\nChangeSource: This attribute is used to store the source of the change that caused the primary driver to be registered or unregistered. This can be either an "API" call or a "Event" from another system.\nOrderID: This attribute is used to store the order ID of the event that caused the primary driver to be registered or unregistered (if applicable).\nEventTimestamp: This attribute is used to store the timestamp when the event that caused the primary driver to be registered or unregistered was emitted (if applicable).\nUserID: This attribute is used to store the user ID of the user that made the update to the primary driver through the API (if applicable). This attribute is only populated if the "Polestar ID Auth API" was used to make the update.\nClientID: This attribute is used to store the client ID of the service that made the update to the primary driver through the API (if applicable). This attribute is only populated if the "M2M Auth API" was used to make the update.\nSystem: This attribute is used to store the name of the system that made the update to the primary driver. This could be the system that emitted the event that caused the change, or the system that made the update through the API.\nIsActive: This attribute is a flag indicating whether the primary driver is currently active or not. If the EndTimestamp is in the past, the attribute is set to false. Otherwise, it is set to true.\nPreviousOrderIDs: This attribute is a list of previous order IDs (if applicable). This is used to determine if the order ID of an incoming event is new or not. If the order ID is present in the list, it is not considered new.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=223, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 14000, 672, 6492, 532, 8616, 529, 506, 13963, 236787, 107, 818, 21264, 161792, 2633, 563, 912, 529, 506, 40088, 8123, 532, 2430