 36%|███▌      | 362/1000 [00:55<01:01, 10.35it/s]INFO 09-15 16:13:03 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-2f21d532e52f4099be4481c7c691b01c-0: prompt: 'Yes, here is an example of refactored Java program that solves the "NoOrderOfOperations" problem by using JUnit test cases to check the results instead of using the main method:\n```\nimport org.junit.Test;\nimport static org.junit.Assert.assertEquals;\n\npublic class NoOrderOfOperations {\n\n    public static int evaluate(String expr) {\n        int result = 0;\n        int current = 0;\n        char operator = \'+\';\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < expr.length(); i++) {\n            char c = expr.charAt(i);\n            if (Character.isDigit(c)) {\n                current = current * 10 + (c - \'0\');\n            } else {\n                result = applyOperator(result, operator, current);\n                operator = c;\n                current = 0;\n            }\n        }\n        result = applyOperator(result, operator, current);\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    private static int applyOperator(int result, char operator, int current) {\n        switch (operator) {\n            case \'+\':\n                return result + current;\n            case \'-\':\n                return result - current;\n            case \'*\':\n                return result * current;\n        }\n        // return the same value if no operator is applied\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    public void testEvaluate() {\n        assertEquals(56, evaluate("3+5*7"));\n        assertEquals(-36, evaluate("4-8*9*1"));\n        assertEquals(0, evaluate("0"));\n        assertEquals(362880, evaluate("1*2*3*4*5*6*7*8*9"));\n    }\n}\n```\nThis refactored program uses JUnit test cases to check the results of the `evaluate` method. The `assertEquals` method is used to check that the returned value of the `evaluate` method is equal to the expected value. JUnit is a framework that makes it easy to write repeatable and automated tests for Java code. This approach makes testing more efficient, as it allows the developer to check all the test cases with a single command.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=10, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 10784, 236764, 1590, 563, 614, 2591, 529, 2123, 773, 2926, 11246, 1948, 600, 64744, 506, 623, 3771, 9067, 4088, 71083, 236775, 2608, 684, 1699, 219213, 1594, 3636, 531, 2426, 506, 2536, 5205, 529, 1699, 506, 1689, 1996, 236787, 107, 2717, 107, 1106, 3447, 236761, 11883, 236761, 3694, 236793, 107, 1106, 2002, 3447, 236761, 11883, 236761, 22042, 236761, 47409, 236793, 108, 2153, 1012, 2301, 9067, 4088, 71083, 642, 108, 140, 2153, 2002, 801, 13901, 236769, 1859, 44103, 236768, 642, 107, 144, 720, 1354, 578, 236743, 236771, 236793, 107, 144, 720, 1873, 578, 236743, 236771, 236793, 107, 144, 4873, 8535, 578, 35587, 2134, 108, 144, 1708, 568, 720, 858, 578, 236743, 236771, 236793, 858, 655, 44103, 236761, 3119, 1086, 858, 4419, 642, 107, 148, 4873, 505, 578, 44103, 236761, 33741, 236769, 236747, 626, 107, 148, 584, 568, 14106, 236761, 511, 48146, 236769, 236755, 1223, 642, 107, 152, 4002, 578, 1873, 808, 236743, 236770, 236771, 900, 568, 236755, 753, 756, 236771, 2106, 107, 148, 236783, 1663, 642, 107, 152, 3709, 578, 5510, 31677, 236769, 3709, 236764, 8535, 236764, 1873, 626, 107, 152, 4132, 578, 505, 236793, 107, 152, 4002, 578, 236743, 236771, 236793, 107, 148, 236783, 107, 144, 236783, 107, 144, 3709, 578, 5510, 31677, 236769, 3709, 236764, 8535, 236764, 1873, 626, 107, 144, 2060, 1354, 236793, 107, 140, 236783, 108, 140, 7128, 2002, 801, 5510, 31677, 236769, 720, 1354,