INFO 09-15 16:13:07 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-617d21fc7cfc40bb9c9b64d9712e8309-0: prompt: "Here is an example implementation of payment gateway integration with a movie booking app using Stripe:\n\n1. Install Stripe API library: The first step is to install the Stripe API library for your programming language. Stripe provides official libraries for many popular programming languages such as Java, Python, and Ruby.\n2. Create a Stripe account: To use Stripe, you will need to create a Stripe account. This will give you access to an API key and other necessary information.\n3. Add Stripe API key: Add the Stripe API key to the movie booking app configuration file.\n4. Create a payment form: Create a payment form that collects the user's payment information such as credit card number, expiration date, and CVV.\n5. Validate payment information: Validate the payment information entered by the user and display any errors.\n6. Submit payment request: When the user submits the payment form, send a request to the Stripe API to create a payment intent.\n7. Confirm payment: After the payment intent is created, the user must confirm the payment. This can be done using the Stripe checkout interface or a custom checkout page.\n8. Handle payment status: After the payment is confirmed, the Stripe API will return a payment status. Handle the payment status to update the movie booking app's database and confirm the user's movie ticket purchase.\n9. Handle payment errors: If the payment fails or is declined, handle the payment error and display a message to the user.\n10. Test payment processing: Test the payment processing system thoroughly before deploying to production to ensure that it is working correctly and reliably.\n\nThis is just an example implementation using Stripe. Other payment gateway providers may have different APIs and integration procedures, but the general process of collecting payment information, submitting a payment request, handling payment status, and testing payment processing remains the same.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=6, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 8291, 563, 614, 2591, 8688, 529, 7548, 44701, 12434, 607, 496, 6387, 22479, 850, 1699, 117377, 236787, 108, 236770, 236761, 18471, 117377, 9299, 9427, 236787, 669, 1171, 2918, 563, 531, 4476, 506, 117377, 9299, 9427, 573, 822, 14929, 5192, 236761, 117377, 4728, 5125, 25027, 573, 1551, 4913, 14929, 15579, 1288, 618, 11246, 236764, 17856, 236764, 532, 46838, 236761, 107, 236778, 236761, 8600, 496, 117377, 2881, 236787, 2282, 1161, 117377, 236764, 611, 795, 1202, 531, 2619, 496, 117377, 2881, 236761, 1174, 795, 2583, 611, 2802, 531, 614, 9299, 2307, 532, 1032, 4127, 1938, 236761, 107, 236800, 236761, 4140, 117377, 9299, 2307, 236787, 4140, 506, 117377, 9299, 2307, 531, 506, 6387, 22479, 850, 9831, 2129, 236761, 107, 236812, 236761, 8600, 496, 7548, 1183, 236787, 8600, 496, 7548, 1183, 600, 60592, 506, 2430, 236789, 236751, 7548, 1938, 1288, 618, 6327, 3733, 1548, 236764, 47763, 3433, 236764, 532, 25572, 236847, 236761, 107, 236810, 236761, 78707, 7548, 1938, 236787, 78707, 506, 7548, 1938, 10708, 684, 506, 2430, 532, 3034, 1027, 9825, 236761, 107, 236825, 236761, 55358, 7548, 2864, 236787, 3026, 506, 2430, 126445, 506, 7548, 1183, 236764, 5039, 496, 2864, 531, 506, 117377, 9299, 531, 2619, 496, 7548, 9703, 236761, 107, 236832, 236761, 64063, 7548, 236787, 4210, 506, 7548, 9703, 563, 4464, 236764, 506, 2430, 1921, 9128, 506, 7548, 236761, 1174, 740, 577, 3028, 1699, 506, 117377, 42290, 7937, 653, 496, 2401, 42290, 3104, 236761, 107, 236828, 236761, 39694, 7548, 4