 40%|████      | 403/1000 [01:01<01:03,  9.47it/s]INFO 09-15 16:13:09 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-2a8faae13d4d495b967a5efd4bf0e8ea-0: prompt: '"Server" is a general term that refers to the computer that stores your application code, receives requests from clients, performs computations, and sends back appropriate responses. In the context of web development, "server" can refer to computers in various locations, such as origin regions, edge networks, or Content Delivery Networks (CDNs).\n\n1. Origin Regions: These are the primary data centers where your application is deployed. The application code resides on servers in these data centers, and they handle requests coming from clients. Origin regions are usually geographically distributed to reduce latency and improve the user experience.\n2. Edge Network: An edge network consists of distributed servers located closer to the users, often at the "edge" of the internet backbone. These servers cache and serve content to reduce latency and offload traffic from the origin servers. Edge networks are often used for caching static assets and serving dynamic content, balancing the load between origin servers and improving the overall performance of an application.\n3. Content Delivery Networks (CDNs): CDNs are a system of distributed servers that deliver content to users based on their geographic location. They help to reduce latency and improve the performance of web applications by caching and serving static assets (e.g., images, stylesheets, JavaScript files) and sometimes even dynamic content from servers closer to the user. This reduces the load on origin servers and speeds up content delivery to end users.\n\nIn the context of rendering, servers in origin regions, edge networks, or CDNs can be responsible for rendering your application code and sending the appropriate response to the client. Depending on your application\'s architecture and deployment, different server locations can be leveraged to optimize performance and reduce latency.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=8, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 236775, 8905, 236775, 563, 496, 2870, 1941, 600, 17230, 531, 506, 5194, 600, 11936, 822, 3739, 3393, 236764, 21500, 10512, 699, 7391, 236764, 28399, 55191, 236764, 532, 25017, 1063, 6780, 13630, 236761, 799, 506, 4403, 529, 4108, 2913, 236764, 623, 6458, 236775, 740, 4029, 531, 19443, 528, 3572, 11024, 236764, 1288, 618, 9059, 9576, 236764, 7377, 12230, 236764, 653, 16748, 33431, 42879, 568, 6329, 51640, 769, 108, 236770, 236761, 45769, 81528, 236787, 3143, 659, 506, 5905, 1262, 16545, 1298, 822, 3739, 563, 29866, 236761, 669, 3739, 3393, 56579, 580, 23367, 528, 1239, 1262, 16545, 236764, 532, 901, 6060, 10512, 4891, 699, 7391, 236761, 45769, 9576, 659, 4781, 110511, 10861, 531, 6439, 51534, 532, 4006, 506, 2430, 2707, 236761, 107, 236778, 236761, 20090, 10981, 236787, 1455, 7377, 3707, 10594, 529, 10861, 23367, 5628, 12532, 531, 506, 5089, 236764, 3187, 657, 506, 623, 9003, 236775, 529, 506, 8379, 58921, 236761, 3143, 23367, 15612, 532, 7298, 3004, 531, 6439, 51534, 532, 1135, 2335, 8827, 699, 506, 9059, 23367, 236761, 20090, 12230, 659, 3187, 1456, 573, 80864, 2002, 10091, 532, 12284, 10795, 3004, 236764, 41346, 506, 3711, 1534, 9059, 23367, 532, 14526, 506, 6782, 3736, 529, 614, 3739, 236761, 107, 236800, 236761, 16748, 33431, 42879, 568, 6329, 51640, 1473, 8080, 51640, 659, 496, 1458, 529, 10861, 23367, 600, 5518, 3004, 531, 5089, 2721, 580, 910, 42442, 4563, 236761, 2195, 1601, 531, 6439, 51534, 532, 4006, 506, 3736, 529, 4108, 6182, 684, 80864, 532, 12284, 2002, 10091, 56