 41%|████▏     | 413/1000 [01:02<01:02,  9.36it/s]INFO 09-15 16:13:10 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-562c0250652745728d0956e993897f31-0: prompt: 'The time complexities of the different scenarios for choosing the pivot in Quick Sort are as follows:\n\n1. First element as pivot: If the input array is already sorted or nearly sorted, choosing the first element as pivot can lead to worst-case time complexity of O(n^2). In the average case, the time complexity is O(nlogn).\n2. Last element as pivot: Similar to the first element as pivot approach, this can lead to worst-case time complexity of O(n^2) in certain scenarios, but has an average time complexity of O(nlogn).\n3. Median element as pivot: This approach guarantees an average time complexity of O(nlogn), but requires finding the median element, which can have a time complexity of O(n).\n4. Random element as pivot: This approach has an average time complexity of O(nlogn), but can lead to worst-case time complexity if the randomly chosen pivot is consistently a bad choice.\n5. Three median as pivot: This approach guarantees a worst-case time complexity of O(nlogn), but has a larger constant factor than the other approaches.\n\nIn general, the choice of pivot depends on the input data and the desired time complexity. In practice, the random pivot approach is commonly used and has good performance in most cases.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=8, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 818, 990, 80116, 529, 506, 1607, 25521, 573, 16890, 506, 38179, 528, 25735, 36702, 659, 618, 5238, 236787, 108, 236770, 236761, 5315, 3408, 61