INFO 09-15 16:13:13 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-1e9e0cb763a2402485bebc4abede74fa-0: prompt: 'To integrate Automated equipment control into the app, we can add the following code:\n```python\nclass Equipment:\n    def __init__(self, equipment_type):\n        self.equipment_type = equipment_type\n        self.status = "off"\n        \n    def turn_on(self):\n        self.status = "on"\n        print(f"{self.equipment_type} is turned on.")\n        \n    def turn_off(self):\n        self.status = "off"\n        print(f"{self.equipment_type} is turned off.")\n        \n        \nclass IrrigationSystem(Equipment):\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__("Irrigation system")\n        self.water_source = None\n        \n    def set_water_source(self, water_source):\n        self.water_source = water_source\n        print(f"Water source is set to {self.water_source}.")\n        \n    def irrigate(self, duration):\n        if self.status == "on":\n            print(f"Irrigating for {duration} minutes with {self.water_source}.")\n        else:\n            print("Cannot irrigate, irrigation system is off.")\n        \n\nclass Harvester(Equipment):\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__("Harvester")\n        self.harvest_type = None\n        \n    def set_harvest_type(self, harvest_type):\n        self.harvest_type = harvest_type\n        print(f"Harvest type is set to {self.harvest_type}.")\n        \n    def harvest(self):\n        if self.status == "on":\n            print(f"Harvesting with {self.harvest_type}.")\n        else:\n            print("Cannot harvest, harvester is off.")\n            \nclass App:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.irrigation_system = IrrigationSystem()\n        self.harvester = Harvester()\n        \n    def control_irrigation_system(self, water_source, duration):\n        self.irrigation_system.set_water_source(water_source)\n        self.irrigation_system.turn_on()\n        self.irrigation_system.irrigate(duration)\n        self.irrigation_system.turn_off()\n        \n    def control_harvester(self, harvest_type):\n        self.harvester.set_harvest_type(harvest_type)\n        self.harvester.turn_on()\n        self.harvester.harvest()\n        self.harvester.turn_off()\n```\nIn the above code, we have created classes for different types of equipment that can be controlled through the app, such as an irrigation system and a harvester. The `Equipment` class is a parent class that contains common attributes and methods for all equipment types. The `IrrigationSystem` and `Harvester` classes inherit from the `Equipment` class and contain additional methods and attributes specific to their respective equipment types.\n\nWe have also created an `App` class that contains methods for controlling the irrigation system and harvester. The `control_irrigation_system` method takes a water source and duration as inputs, sets the water source for the irrigation system, turns it on, irrigates for the specified duration, and turns it off. The `control_harvester` method takes a harvest type as input, sets the harvest type for the harvester, turns it on, harvests the crops, and turns it off.\n\nThese methods can be called by the app to control the equipment and automate farm operations.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=63, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2021, 25139, 94770, 5842, 2256, 1131, 506, 850, 236764, 692, 740, 1138, 506, 2269, 3393, 236787, 107, 2717, 6719, 107, 1999, 29187, 236787, 107, 140, 2063, 5062, 2949, 10210, 1508, 236764, 5842, 236779, 2084, 1473, 107, 144, 1508, 236761, 89149