INFO 09-15 16:13:16 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-ecf78349d23a4ae4b36c7e3b4aeb57e4-0: prompt: "Case Study 1: Alice, an elderly patient\nAlice is an 85-year-old patient who has been bedridden for several weeks after a hip replacement surgery. She has developed a pressure injury on her buttocks, which is not healing. She has a history of diabetes and is at risk of developing further complications.\n\nTasks:\n\n1. Assess the pressure injury using the National Pressure Injury Advisory Panel (NPIAP) guidelines.\n2. Identify the risk factors contributing to Alice's pressure injury.\n3. Develop a treatment plan for Alice's pressure injury, including wound dressing and pressure relief devices.\n4. Educate Alice and her family on the importance of pressure injury prevention and management, including turning and repositioning techniques.\n5. Document the assessment, treatment plan, and education in Alice's medical records.\n\nResources:\n\n* NPIAP guidelines for pressure injury assessment\n* Pressure injury treatment algorithms\n* Pressure relief devices information sheet\n* Turning and repositioning techniques information sheet\n* Documentation template for pressure injury assessment and management\n\nCase Study 2: Tom, a middle-aged patient\nTom is a 50-year-old patient who is recovering from a spinal cord injury. He is partially paralyzed and has limited mobility. He has developed a pressure injury on his back, which is not healing.\n\nTasks:\n\n1. Assess the pressure injury using the NPIAP guidelines.\n2. Identify the risk factors contributing to Tom's pressure injury.\n3. Develop a treatment plan for Tom's pressure injury, including wound dressing and pressure relief devices.\n4. Implement a turning and repositioning schedule for Tom to prevent further pressure injuries.\n5. Educate Tom and his family on the importance of pressure injury prevention and management.\n6. Document the assessment, treatment plan, and education in Tom's medical records.\n\nResources:\n\n* NPIAP guidelines for pressure injury assessment\n* Pressure injury treatment algorithms\n* Pressure relief devices information sheet\n* Turning and repositioning techniques information sheet\n* Documentation template for pressure injury assessment and management\n\nCase Study 3: Liam, a young patient\nLiam is a 25-year-old patient who has been involved in a car accident and has a spinal cord injury. He is at high risk of developing pressure injuries due to his immobility.\n\nTasks:\n\n1. Assess Liam's risk of developing pressure injuries using the Braden Scale.\n2. Develop a prevention plan for Liam's pressure injuries, including turning and repositioning schedule, pressure relief devices, and skin care.\n3. Educate Liam and his family on pressure injury prevention and management.\n4. Document the risk assessment, prevention plan, and education in Liam's medical records.\n\nResources:\n\n* Braden Scale for predicting pressure sore risk\n* Pressure injury prevention plan template\n* Turning and repositioning techniques information sheet\n* Pressure relief devices information sheet\n* Skin care information sheet\n* Documentation template for pressure injury prevention and management", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=14, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 9818, 16785, 236743, 236770, 236787, 32858, 236764, 614, 24831, 6213, 107, 85305, 563, 614, 236743, 236828, 236810, 236772, 3704, 236772, 947, 6213, 1015, 815, 1010, 4086, 81729, 573, 3131, 5695, 1308, 496, 16240, 14268, 13625, 236761, 2625, 815, 5535, 496, 4204, 9938, 580, 1116, 175797, 236764, 837, 563, 711, 21123, 236761,