INFO 09-15 16:13:20 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-b1488e128fb64b98b11b5d187a6eecd0-0: prompt: "Thank you for providing the additional information. With the information you've provided, I can provide an example of a letter that could be used to accompany an H-1B visa application for Ugne Karaliute.\n\n[Employer Name]\n[Employer Address]\n[City, State ZIP Code]\n[Employer Phone Number]\n[Employer Email]\n\n[Date]\n\nUnited States Citizenship and Immigration Services\n[USCIS Address]\n[City, State ZIP Code]\n\nSubject: H-1B Visa Petition for Ugne Karaliute\n\nDear Sir/Madam,\n\nI am writing to petition for the H-1B nonimmigrant visa classification for Ugne Karaliute, who will be working as a [insert job title] at [Employer Name]. Our company is in need of a highly skilled and qualified individual with expertise in [insert field of expertise], and we believe that Ugne is the perfect candidate for this position.\n\nUgne has a [insert degree level] degree in [insert field of study], which is directly relevant to the specialty occupation of [insert job title]. In addition, Ugne has [insert number] years of experience in [insert field of expertise] and has a solid track record of accomplishments in this field.\n\nUgne will be working on a full-time basis for [Employer Name] and will be responsible for [insert job duties]. Our company is committed to providing Ugne with a competitive salary and benefits package, and we will ensure that he is paid at least the actual or prevailing wage for the occupation, whichever is higher.\n\nWe are confident that Ugne will make a valuable contribution to our company and we look forward to welcoming him to the United States to begin working on this important project.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration.\n\nSincerely,\n\n[Your Name]\n[Your Title]\n[Employer Name]\n\nEnclosures:\n\n* Form I-129, Petition for a Nonimmigrant Worker\n* Ugne Karaliute's resume and qualifications\n* Evidence of the company's ability to pay the offered wage\n* Labor Condition Application (LCA) certified by the U.S. Department of Labor\n* Any other relevant supporting documents\n\nPlease note that this is just an example and may not be suitable for actual use. The information and documents needed for H-1B visa application can vary depending on the case, and it is always best to consult with an immigration lawyer or professional for further guidance and assistance.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=5, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 14782, 611, 573, 6655, 506, 4767, 1938, 236761, 3227, 506, 1938, 611, 236789, 560, 3847, 236764, 564, 740, 2847, 614, 2591, 529, 496, 6064, 600, 1451, 577, 1456, 531, 23714, 614, 640, 236772, 236770, 236799, 33485, 3739, 573, 34151, 866, 9953, 3555, 1328, 236761, 108, 236840, 225898, 7343, 236842, 107, 236840, 225898, 15874, 236842, 107, 236840, 17698, 236764, 3245, 65911, 8739, 236842, 107, 236840, 225898, 23386, 9661, 236842, 107, 236840, 225898, 19955, 236842, 108, 236840, 3682, 236842, 108, 27211, 4184, 111661, 532, 73031, 8381, 107, 236840, 3118, 149531, 15874, 236842, 107, 236840, 17698, 236764, 3245, 65911, 8739, 236842, 108, 21288, 236787, 640, 236772, 236770, 236799, 39544, 99136, 573, 34151, 866, 9953, 3555, 1328, 108, 31163, 12182, 236786, 195889, 236764, 108, 236777, 1006, 5712, 531, 14071, 573, 506, 640, 236772, 236770, 236799, 1908, 9411, 126469, 33485, 15241, 573, 34151, 866, 9953, 3555, 1328, 236764, 1015, 795, 577, 2844, 618, 496, 870, 9397, 3195, 3822, 236842, 657, 870, 225898, 7343, 1619, 5137, 2544, 563, 528, 1202, 529, 496, 6112, 23482, 532, 15973, 3141, 607, 14739, 52