INFO 09-15 16:13:21 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-e4b69a0c1f1342708766fdef7e4d989e-0: prompt: "B) Inaccuracy in identifying relevant clinical concepts is a limitation of natural language processing (NLP) in healthcare. NLP refers to the ability of computers to process and understand human language. In healthcare, NLP can be used to extract relevant clinical information from unstructured text, such as clinical notes or radiology reports. However, NLP algorithms may not always accurately identify relevant clinical concepts due to variations in terminology, syntax, and context.\n\nA) Inability to process unstructured data is not a limitation of NLP in healthcare, as one of the main applications of NLP is to extract clinical information from unstructured text.\n\nC) Limited availability of NLP tools and resources is not a limitation of NLP in healthcare, as there are many commercially available and open-source NLP tools and resources that can be used in healthcare applications.\n\nD) High cost of implementing NLP systems may be a practical limitation for some healthcare organizations, but it is not an inherent limitation of NLP in healthcare.\n\nThis question corresponds to the Analysis level of Bloom's Taxonomy, as it requires an understanding of the limitations of NLP in healthcare and the ability to evaluate the relevance of each option.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=71, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 236799, 236768, 799, 28611, 528, 21558, 7798, 9737, 14485, 563, 496, 26919, 529, 3756, 5192, 8487, 568, 163155, 236768, 528, 16106, 236761, 103284, 17230, 531, 506