INFO 09-15 16:13:24 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-60a1a049b4684762ac87de48abef2d39-0: prompt: 'I am going to give you some questions with multiple choice answers, answer them, while rewriting all of the questions and citing which is the right answer for each question : \n\n1. Why is the Cobden-Chevalier Treaty considered a milestone in international political economy?\n\n- Because it legalized the Gold Standard \n- Because it recognised the interconnectedness of monetary and trade relations\n- Because it established the repeal of the Corn Laws\n- Because it included a most-favored nations clause\n\n2. Which of the following is NOT specified by the Reciprocal Trade Agreements Act?\n\n- The U.S. Presidential administration is in charge of trade negotiations \n- The U.S. President can propose bilateral, reciprocal tariff reductions\n- The U.S. Congress can amend trade agreements \n- The U.S. Congress ratifies trade agreements\n\n3. According to Friedrich List, private interests\n\n- generally coincide with public interests and promote wealth \n- are more important than public interests \n- often conflict with public interests \n- help to promote the development of a country', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=451, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 236777, 1006, 1771, 531, 2583, 611, 1070, 4137, 607, 5065, 5313, 12102, 236764, 3890, 1091, 236764, 1651, 111465, 784, 529, 506, 4137, 532, 47003, 837, 563, 506, 1447, 3890, 573, 1546, 2934, 1017, 236743, 108, 236770, 236761, 8922, 563, 506, 38379, 2235, 236772, 5239, 1111, 1099, 59295, 4542, 496, 47722, 528, 5251, 5255, 8122, 23