 54%|█████▍    | 542/1000 [01:18<00:48,  9.38it/s]INFO 09-15 16:13:25 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-6e83e6a54ecd407d8cc2b5fec0b1ae31-0: prompt: 'To run the `curl` command, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Open a terminal or command prompt on your computer.\n2. Type the `curl` command with the appropriate options and arguments. Here is an example command that sends a POST request to the recipe generator API:\n```json\ncurl -X POST \\\n     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\\n     -d \'{"ingredients": ["chicken", "rice", "vegetables"]}\' \\\n     http://localhost:5000/generate_recipe\n```\nThis command sends a POST request to the `http://localhost:5000/generate_recipe` URL with a JSON payload containing the list of ingredients.\n\nNote that if you are running the API on a different server or port, you will need to update the URL accordingly.\n3. Press enter to execute the `curl` command. The response from the API will appear in the terminal.\n\nThe response should be a JSON object containing the recipe information, like this:\n```swift\n{\n    "name": "Chicken Fried Rice",\n    "ingredients": [\n        {\n            "id": 1015062,\n            "name": "vegetable oil",\n            "amount": 2.0,\n            "unit": "tablespoons"\n        },\n        {\n            "id": 1123,\n            "name": "chicken breasts",\n            "amount": 2.0,\n            "unit": ""\n        },\n        {\n            "id": 20444,\n            "name": "frozen peas and carrots",\n            "amount": 1.0,\n            "unit": "cup"\n        },\n        {\n            "id": 10220445,\n            "name": "cooked white rice",\n            "amount": 3.0,\n            "unit": "cups"\n        },\n        {\n            "id": 11215,\n            "name": "egg",\n            "amount": 2.0,\n            "unit": ""\n        },\n        {\n            "id": 16124,\n            "name": "soy sauce",\n            "amount": 2.0,\n            "unit": "tablespoons"\n        },\n        {\n            "id": 1002050,\n            "name": "salt",\n            "amount": 0.5,\n            "unit": "teaspoon"\n        },\n        {\n            "id": 10019903,\n            "name": "black pepper",\n            "amount": 0.5,\n            "unit": "teaspoon"\n        }\n    ],\n    "instructions": "1. Heat 1 tablespoon of vegetable oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the chicken and cook for 5-6 minutes until cooked through. Remove from the skillet and set aside.\\n2. Add the remaining tablespoon of vegetable oil to the skillet. Add the peas and carrots and cook for 2-3 minutes until tender.\\n3. Add the cooked rice to the skillet and stir to combine with the vegetables. Push the rice mixture to the side of the skillet.\\n4. Add the beaten eggs to the empty side of the skillet and scramble until cooked.\\n5. Combine the rice and eggs and add the cooked chicken back to the skillet. Add the soy sauce, salt, and black pepper and stir to combine. Serve hot.",\n    "cooking_time": 30,\n    "servings": 4,\n    "cuisine": [\n        "Chinese",\n        "Asian"\n    ],\n    "difficulty": "easy",\n    "dietary_restrictions": [\n        "dairy-free"\n    ]\n}\n```\nIf the API cannot find any recipes with the given ingredients, the response will contain a 404 error', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=9, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2021, 1845, 506, 2165, 40192, 236929, 4991, 236764, 611, 740, 1500, 1239, 6555, 236787, 108, 236770, 236761, 7607, 496, 12612, 653, 4991, 11172, 580, 822, 5194, 236761, 107, 236778, 236761, 9250, 506, 2165, 40192, 236929, 4991, 607, 506,