 56%|█████▌    | 559/1000 [01:22<04:00,  1.83it/s]INFO 09-15 16:13:30 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-f0fe3ab07055443fb884031069e5b2b7-0: prompt: 'Here is an example of how to generate a synthetic input and output dataset based on the literature and save it as an Excel file:\n```{r}\nlibrary(tibble)\nlibrary(dplyr)\nlibrary(writexl)\n\n# Set the working directory to the desired directory where you want to save the file\nsetwd("C:/Users/YourUserName/Documents/YourFolder")\n\n# Generate a synthetic input dataset\ninput_data <- tibble(\n  Temperature = runif(10, 5, 30),\n  Moisture = runif(10, 0.2, 0.4),\n  Nitrate = runif(10, 5, 50),\n  Carbon = runif(10, 20, 200),\n  Oxygen = runif(10, 1, 10)\n)\n\n# Define the model parameters\nKc <- 0.05  # Empirical rate constant for denitrification\nKo <- 0.2   # Empirical rate constant for oxygen inhibition\n\n# Calculate the N2O emissions based on the input dataset\noutput_data <- input_data %>%\n  mutate(\n    Denitrification_Rate = Kc * Nitrate * Carbon / (Nitrate + Kc) * exp(-Ko * Oxygen),\n    N2O_Emissions = Denitrification_Rate * 0.01  # Assume 1% of denitrified N is emitted as N2O\n  )\n\n# Save the input and output data as separate sheets in an Excel file\nwrite_xlsx(list("Input Data" = input_data, "Output Data" = output_data), "synthetic_data.xlsx")\n```\nIn this example, the `setwd()` function sets the working directory to `C:/Users/YourUserName/Documents/YourFolder`. You can change this path to the desired directory where you want to save the file. The `write_xlsx()` function is used to save the input and output data as separate sheets in an Excel file called "synthetic\\_data.xlsx" in the current working directory. The input data is generated using the `runif()` function to generate random values for temperature, moisture, nitrate, carbon, and oxygen. The output data is calculated based on the input data using the denitrification model equations from the literature, assuming a fixed rate constant for denitrification and oxygen inhibition, and assuming that 1% of denitrified N is emitted as N2O.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=14, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 8291, 563, 614, 2591, 529, 1217, 531, 8729, 496, 22615, 2744, 532, 3938, 15297, 2721, 580, 506, 11089, 532, 5383, 625, 618, 614, 20824, 2129, 236787, 107, 230956, 236750, 236783, 107, 12195, 236769, 223273, 1148, 236768, 107, 12195, 236769, 102764, 236768, 107, 12195, 236769, 101354, 716, 236752, 236768, 108, 236865, 5833, 506, 2844, 12229, 531, 506, 10991, 12229, 1298, 611, 1461, 531, 5383, 506, 2129, 107, 160824, 885, 236780, 23932, 13465, 236786, 11069, 62312, 236786, 41250, 236786, 11069, 13119, 1373, 108, 236865, 43550, 496, 22615, 2744, 15297, 107, 2427, 236779, 1516, 4778, 48799, 1148, 236769, 107, 138, 51994, 578, 1845, 584, 236769, 236770, 236771, 236764, 236743, 236810, 236764, 236743, 236800, 236771, 779, 107, 138, 18557, 199316, 578, 1845, 584, 236769, 236770, 236771, 236764, 236743, 236771, 236761, 236778, 236764, 236743, 236771, 236761, 236812, 779, 107, 138, 62486, 4720, 578, 1845, 584, 236769, 236770, 236771, 236764, 236743, 236810, 236764, 236743, 236810, 236771, 779, 107, 138, 71275, 578, 1845, 584, 236769, 236770, 236771, 236764, 236743, 236778, 236771, 236764, 236743, 236778, 236771, 236771, 779, 107, 138, 170701, 578, 1845, 584, 236769, 236770, 236771, 236764, 236743, 236770, 236764, 236743, 236770, 236771, 236768, 107, 236768, 108, 236865, 31238, 506, 2028, 6137, 107, 198845, 4778, 236743, 236771, 236761, 236771, 236810, 138, 236865, 161936, 3136, 4512, 573, 141551, 107, 42214, 4778, 236743, 236771