INFO 09-15 16:13:30 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-11769c3673c34e3d947690dcc8db3dec-0: prompt: "There is no scientific evidence connecting the Transverse temporal gyrus to the inner voice or the voice of God. However, the Transverse temporal gyrus, also known as Heschl's gyrus, is an important structure in the processing of auditory information in the brain, as it is the first cortical structure to process incoming auditory information [[1](https://alchetron.com/Transverse-temporal-gyrus)]. The gyrus is located in the primary auditory cortex, which is responsible for the initial processing of sound [[3](https://www.kenhub.com/en/library/anatomy/auditory-pathway)].\n\nIn terms of the occult, some spiritual traditions and belief systems posit that the inner voice or the voice of God can be accessed through meditation, prayer, or other forms of spiritual practice. Some practitioners may associate this experience with specific brain regions, including the Transverse temporal gyrus, although there is no scientific evidence to support this claim.\n\nIn conclusion, while the Transverse temporal gyrus plays an important role in auditory processing, there is no scientific evidence connecting it to the inner voice or the voice of God. Any claims linking the gyrus to spiritual experiences or beliefs are not supported by scientific evidence.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=21, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 3810, 563, 951, 11639, 4914, 18024, 506, 4215, 3929, 25216, 549, 47968, 531, 506, 9628, 8300, 653, 506, 8300, 529, 3803, 236761, 3153, 236764, 506, 4215, 3929, 25216, 549,