 58%|█████▊    | 583/1000 [01:27<01:29,  4.68it/s]INFO 09-15 16:13:35 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-5ebb2fa9e46b439c85421d14ee8e5b7b-0: prompt: '2. "Fixed Points and Stability of Nonlinear Neural Networks," by M.A. S. Kamal and A. Ahmed, 2013 - This paper analyzes the fixed points and stability of nonlinear neural networks, providing insights into their behavior and convergence properties.\n3. "Deep Learning," by Y. LeCun, Y. Bengio, and G. Hinton, 2015 - This paper provides an overview of deep learning, including its history, current state, and future prospects.\n4. "A guide to convolution arithmetic for deep learning," by V. Dumoulin and F. Visin, 2018 - This paper provides a comprehensive guide to the arithmetic of convolutional neural networks, which are commonly used in deep learning for image processing.\n5. "Matrix Analysis and Applied Linear Algebra," by C.D. Meyer, 2000 - This book provides a comprehensive introduction to matrix analysis and its applications in linear algebra.\n6. "The Matrix Cookbook," by K.B. Petersen and M.S. Pedersen, 2006 - This book provides a collection of matrix identities and other results useful for linear algebra and matrix analysis.\n7. "Recurrent Neural Networks Tutorial, Part 4 - Implementing a GRU/LSTM RNN with Python and Theano," by D. Britz, 2015 - This tutorial provides a practical guide to implementing recurrent neural networks using Python and Theano, with a focus on gated recurrent unit and long short-term memory networks.\n8. "Dropout: A Simple Way to Prevent Neural Networks from Overfitting," by N. Srivastava, G. Hinton, A. Krizhevsky, I. Sutskever, and R. Salakhutdinov, 2014 - This paper introduces the dropout regularization technique for preventing overfitting in neural networks.\n9. "Batch Normalization: Accelerating Deep Network Training by Reducing Internal Covariate Shift," by S. Ioffe and C. Szegedy, 2015 - This paper introduces the batch normalization technique for improving the stability and convergence of deep neural networks.\n10. "An overview of gradient descent optimization algorithms," by S. Ruder, 2016 - This paper provides an overview of various optimization algorithms for training neural networks using gradient descent.\n11. "A brief survey of deep learning," by L. Deng and D. Yu, 2014 - This paper provides a survey of deep learning techniques, including convolutional neural networks, recurrent neural networks, and deep belief networks.\n12. "Understanding the difficulty of training deep feedforward neural networks," by X. Glorot and Y. Bengio, 2010 - This paper provides insights into the difficulty of training deep feedforward neural networks, and proposes solutions for improving their training and convergence.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=11, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 236778, 236761, 623, 22140, 36526, 532, 69489, 529, 85687, 63295, 42879, 2098, 684, 587, 236761, 236776, 236761, 555, 236761, 115041, 532, 562, 236761, 36315, 236764, 236743, 236778, 236771, 236770, 236800, 753, 1174, 3627, 73994, 506, 6530, 3298, 532, 11646, 529, 23388, 22823, 12230, 236764, 6655, 19317, 1131, 910, 6868, 532, 22861, 5082, 236761, 107, 236800, 236761, 623, 39300, 19180, 2098, 684, 895, 236761, 1834, 236780, 602, 236764, 895, 236761, 24038, 897, 236764, 532, 667, 236761, 216553, 236764, 236743, 236778, 236771, 236770, 236810, 753, 1174, 3627, 4728, 614, 21385, 529, 5268, 4735, 236764, 2440, 1061, 4083, 236764, 1873, 1883, 236764, 532, 3402, 28541, 236761, 107, 236812, 236761, 623, 236776, 8214, 531, 51457, 40442, 573, 5268, 4735, 2098, 684, 782, 236761, 59421, 521, 3775