INFO 09-15 16:13:36 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-c2aa72a21807447a9709ac975549d9e7-0: prompt: 'you to leverage the benefits of JSON and modern templating engines, while still maintaining the visual formatting you require.\n\n1. Apply CSS styles: After creating the HTML template and rendering the content, you can apply CSS styles to achieve the desired appearance for your XML data. This can be done by adding CSS classes to the elements in your template and defining corresponding styles in a stylesheet.\n\nFor example, if you want to style the list items in the previous example, you could update the template with a CSS class:\n```html\n<ul>\n  {{#each items}}\n    <li class="styled-item">{{subelement}}</li>\n  {{/each}}\n</ul>\n```\nAnd then define the CSS style in a stylesheet:\n```css\n.styled-item {\n  color: #333;\n  font-weight: bold;\n  /* Add any additional styles you need */\n}\n```\nThis approach allows you to separate the structure of your content (HTML) from its presentation (CSS), making it easier to maintain and update your visual formatting in the future.\n\nBy combining JSON, a modern templating engine, and CSS, you can achieve similar visual formatting for your XML chunks as you had with XSL, while utilizing modern web technologies that are more maintainable and compatible with different browsers.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=112, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 7624, 531, 30990, 506, 6417, 529, 10434, 532, 4532, 92054, 1194, 18362, 236764, 1651, 2036, 16977, 506, 7426, 53892, 611, 1660, 236761, 108, 236770, 236761, 30839, 22940, 14062, 236787, 42