 60%|█████▉    | 598/1000 [01:29<00:41,  9.72it/s]INFO 09-15 16:13:37 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-d45ff80bae0648a7876872828637218c-0: prompt: 'In Python, code running from the same interpreter can import and use loggers that have been created or configured in other parts of the code. This allows different parts of the code to share and use the same logger instance, which can simplify logging and make it easier to manage and configure log output.\n\nFor example, if an engineer creates a logger in the main part of their code, they can import and use that logger in a separate function or module that is called by the main code. This allows the code running in the separate function or module to use the same logger instance, which means that log messages will be written to the same output and use the same configuration as the logger in the main code.\n\nOverall, code running from the same interpreter can import and use loggers that have been created or configured in other parts of the code, which can simplify logging and improve the management of log output.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=11, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 902, 17856, 236764, 3393, 4710, 699, 506, 1638, 56714, 740, 1419, 532, 1161, 2212, 9964, 600, 735, 1010, 4464, 653, 28331, 528, 1032, 4688, 529, 506, 3393, 236761, 1174, 5862, 1607, 4688, 529, 506, 3393, 531, 4024, 532, 1161, 506, 1638, 17296, 5705, 236764, 837, 740, 30091, 19346, 532, 1386, 625, 8722, 531, 9688, 532, 26955, 2212, 3938, 236761, 108, 2542, 2591, 236764, 768, 614, 19042, 14004, 496, 17296, 528, 506, 1689, 912, 529, 910, 3393, 236764