 60%|██████    | 600/1000 [01:30<00:45,  8.87it/s]INFO 09-15 16:13:37 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-db7de4758b6a45fe8acae15500718f86-0: prompt: 'Sure, here is an example of a simple snake game made with the ezsgame library:\n```python\nfrom ezsgame import *\nimport random\n\n# Initialize the window\nwindow = Window(title="Snake Game - (Code Sample)", show_fps=True)\n\n# Initialize the snake\nsnake = Rect(\n    pos=Pos("center", "center"),\n    size=(20, 20),\n    color="white"\n)\n\n# Initialize the food\nfood = Circle(\n    pos=Pos(random.randint(0, window.size.width), random.randint(0, window.size.height)),\n    radius=5,\n    color="red"\n)\n\n# Initialize the snake\'s direction\ndirection = "right"\n\n# Initialize the snake\'s tail\ntail = []\n\n# Main game loop\nwhile True:\n    window.check_events()\n\n    # Clear the screen\n    window.fill("black")\n\n    # Update the snake\'s position based on its direction\n    if direction == "right":\n        snake.pos.x += snake.size.width\n    elif direction == "left":\n        snake.pos.x -= snake.size.width\n    elif direction == "up":\n        snake.pos.y -= snake.size.height\n    elif direction == "down":\n        snake.pos.y += snake.size.height\n\n    # Add the snake\'s current position to its tail\n    tail.append(snake.pos.copy())\n    if len(tail) > 5:\n        tail.pop(0)\n\n    # Check if the snake has collided with the food\n    if snake.colliderect(food):\n        food.pos = Pos(random.randint(0, window.size.width), random.randint(0, window.size.height))\n        tail.append(snake.pos.copy())\n\n    # Draw the food\n    food.draw()\n\n    # Draw the snake\'s tail\n    for i in range(len(tail)):\n        rect = Rect(\n            pos=tail[i],\n            size=(20, 20),\n            color="white"\n        )\n        rect.draw()\n\n    # Draw the snake\n    snake.draw()\n\n    # Update the window\n    window.update()\n```\nIn this example, we use the `Rect` and `Circle` classes to create the snake and food objects respectively. We use the `Pos` class to position the snake and food on the screen. We also use a while loop to run the game, and check for user inputs to change the direction of the snake. The snake is also has a tail that is represented by a list of rectangles, and the snake eats the food which generates a new food in random location on the screen.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=28, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 49190, 236764, 1590, 563, 614, 2591, 529, 496, 3606, 22825, 2290, 1603, 607, 506, 24846, 236751, 5567, 9427, 236787, 107, 2717, 6719, 107, 2543, 24846, 236751, 5567, 1419, 808, 107, 1106, 4940, 108, 236865, 28392, 506, 4771, 107, 7414, 578, 28405, 236769, 3250, 718, 67242, 9064, 753, 568, 4809, 31278, 22730, 1407, 236779, 40426, 236784, 4339, 236768, 108, 236865, 28392, 506, 22825, 107, 37942, 578, 41733, 236769, 107, 140, 1163, 236784, 10274, 885, 3873, 827, 623, 3873, 3959, 107, 140, 2086, 9036, 236778, 236771, 236764, 236743, 236778, 236771, 779, 107, 140, 3001, 718, 7986, 236775, 107, 236768, 108, 236865, 28392, 506, 2780, 107, 17625, 578, 28260, 236769, 107, 140, 1163, 236784, 10274, 236769, 7513, 236761, 33156, 236769, 236771, 236764, 4771, 236761, 2086, 236761, 2690, 779, 4940, 236761, 33156, 236769, 236771, 236764, 4771, 236761, 2086, 236761, 4603, 8914, 107, 140, 12485, 236784, 236810, 236764, 107, 140, 3001, 718, 1192, 236775, 107, 236768, 108, 236865, 28392, 506, 22825, 236789, 236751, 5281, 107, 16145, 578, 623, 898, 236775, 108, 236865, 28392, 506, 22825, 236789, 236751, 9743, 107, 14170, 578, 2977, 108, 236865, 6400, 2290, 7350, 10