INFO 09-15 16:13:42 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-5fdad59c70c243658745ef54a12bd7f0-0: prompt: 'Sure! Here\'s the updated code with Roberta base model and EarlyStoppingCallback added:\n```python\nfrom transformers import RobertaForSequenceClassification, RobertaTokenizerFast\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import KFold\nfrom datasets import load_dataset\nfrom transformers import TrainingArguments, Trainer, EarlyStoppingCallback\n\n# Load dataset\ndataset = load_dataset("csv", data_files={"train": "./data/train.csv", "validation": "./data/val.csv"}, delimiter=",")\n\n# Load tokenizer and encode the dataset\ntokenizer = RobertaTokenizerFast.from_pretrained(\'roberta-base\')\ndef encode_dataset(d):\n    return tokenizer(d[\'text\'], padding=\'max_length\', truncation=True, max_length=512)\ndataset = dataset.map(encode_dataset)\n\n# Define training arguments\ntraining_args = TrainingArguments(\n    output_dir=\'./results\',          # output directory\n    num_train_epochs=3,              # total number of training epochs\n    per_device_train_batch_size=32,  # batch size per device during training\n    per_device_eval_batch_size=64,   # batch size for evaluation\n    warmup_steps=500,                # number of warmup steps for learning rate scheduler\n    weight_decay=0.01,               # strength of weight decay\n    logging_dir=\'./logs\',            # directory for storing logs\n    logging_steps=10,\n    evaluation_strategy=\'epoch\',     # evaluation strategy to adopt during training\n    save_total_limit=3,              # maximum number of checkpoints to save\n    eval_steps=None,                 # number of steps between evaluations\n    save_strategy=\'epoch\',           # save checkpoint every eval_steps\n    load_best_model_at_end=True,     # load the best model when finished training\n    metric_for_best_model=\'accuracy\',# use accuracy to evaluate the best model\n    early_stopping_patience=2        # stop training early if no improvement for 2 evaluations\n)\n\n# Define k-fold cross-validation\nkfold = KFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\n\nfor fold, (train_indices, val_indices) in enumerate(kfold.split(dataset)):\n    # Split the dataset into train and validation sets for this fold\n    train_dataset = dataset.select(train_indices)\n    val_dataset = dataset.select(val_indices)\n\n    # Load model and prepare the Trainer\n    model = RobertaForSequenceClassification.from_pretrained(\'roberta-base\', num_labels=8)\n\n    trainer = Trainer(\n        model=model,\n        args=training_args,\n        train_dataset=train_dataset,\n        eval_dataset=val_dataset,\n        compute_metrics=lambda p: {\'accuracy\': (p.predictions.argmax(axis=-1) == p.label_ids).mean()},\n        callbacks=[EarlyStoppingCallback(early_stopping_patience=2)]  # add EarlyStoppingCallback\n    )\n\n    # Train the model for this fold\n    trainer.train()\n```\nNote that the `EarlyStoppingCallback` is added to the `callbacks` argument of the `Trainer` object with `early_stopping_patience` set to 2. This means that the training will be stopped early if the evaluation metric does not improve for 2 consecutive evaluations on the validation set.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=46, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 49190, 236888, 5715, 236789, 236751, 506, 10448, 3393, 607, 139810, 3225, 2028, 532, 21107, 158224, 14217, 3742, 236787, 107, 2717, 6719, 107, 2543, 39687, 1419, 139810, 2542, 35997, 76490, 236764, 139810, 79597, 37568, 107, 2543, 22250, 236761, 4368, 236779, 22806, 1419, 751, 39229, 107, 2543, 32542, 1419, 3711, 236779, 1774