 67%|██████▋   | 666/1000 [01:39<01:01,  5.42it/s]INFO 09-15 16:13:46 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-81bb0c0f04d84732ab3a1a25208ace25-0: prompt: "In Linux, you can find and kill the process using a specific port with the following steps:\n\n1. Open a terminal window.\n2. Run the following command to find the process ID (PID) of the process using the port:\n```bash\nsudo lsof -i :<port>\n```\nReplace `<port>` with the port number you want to check. For example, to find the process using port 8080, the command would be:\n```bash\nsudo lsof -i :8080\n```\n1. Look for the line showing the process name and the PID. The PID will be in the second column.\n2. Use the `kill` command to terminate the process by its PID:\n```bash\nsudo kill <PID>\n```\nReplace `<PID>` with the process ID you found in step 3.\n\nFor example, if the PID is 1234, the command would be:\n```bash\nsudo kill 1234\n```\nIf the process doesn't terminate with the regular `kill` command, you can forcefully terminate it using the `kill -9` command:\n```bash\nsudo kill -9 <PID>\n```\nThis will forcefully terminate the process,", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=18, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 902, 21694, 236764, 611, 740, 1586, 532, 11807, 506, 1657, 1699, 496, 3530, 2411, 607, 506, 2269, 6555, 236787, 108, 236770, 236761, 7607, 496, 12612, 4771, 236761, 107, 236778, 236761, 9793, 506, 2269, 4991, 531, 1586, 506, 1657, 5853, 568, 105300, 236768, 529, 506, 1657, 1699, 506, 2411, 236787, 107, 2717, 42422, 107, 49629, 537, 86095, 753, 236747, 1017, 236820, 728, 236813, 107, 2717, 107, 42762, 41209, 728, 672