INFO 09-15 16:13:48 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-4774f213b5c9489a84137cd23042accd-0: prompt: "Sure! Here's the code for part i:\n```python\n# Load test data\ntest_data = []\nfor i in range(19, 21):\n    rgb = cv2.imread(f'./onions/{i:02d}_rgb.png')\n    depth = cv2.imread(f'./onions/{i:02d}_depth.png', cv2.IMREAD_GRAYSCALE)\n    truth = cv2.imread(f'./onions/{i:02d}_truth.png', cv2.IMREAD_GRAYSCALE)\n    test_data.append((rgb, depth, truth))\n\n# Calculate features for test data\ntest_features = []\nfor rgb, depth, truth in test_data:\n    onion_patches, weed_patches = extract_patches(rgb, depth, truth)\n    onion_features = calculate_features(onion_patches)\n    weed_features = calculate_features(weed_patches)\n    test_features.append((onion_features, weed_features))\n\n# Test model on test data\nfor i, (onion_features, weed_features) in enumerate(test_features):\n    # Shape features only\n    test_X = np.vstack((onion_features[:, :4], weed_features[:, :4]))\n    test_y = np.hstack((np.zeros(len(onion_features)), np.ones(len(weed_features))))\n    test_X_scaled = scaler.transform(test_X)\n    preds = clf_shape.predict(test_X_scaled)\n    report = classification_report(test_y, preds, target_names=['onion', 'weed'], output_dict=True)\n    print(f'Test Results for Sample {i+19} using Shape Features Only:\\n{report}')\n\n    # Texture features only\n    test_X = np.vstack((onion_features[:, 4:], weed_features[:, 4:]))\n    test_y = np.hstack((np.zeros(len(onion_features)), np.ones(len(weed_features))))\n    test_X_scaled = scaler.transform(test_X)\n    preds = clf_texture.predict(test_X_scaled)\n    report = classification_report(test_y, preds, target_names=['onion', 'weed'], output_dict=True)\n    print(f'Test Results for Sample {i+19} using Texture Features Only:\\n{report}')\n\n    # Combined shape and texture features\n    test_X = np.hstack((onion_features, weed_features))\n    test_y = np.hstack((np.zeros(len(onion_features)), np.ones(len(weed_features))))\n    test_X_scaled = scaler.transform(test_X)\n    preds = clf_combined.predict(test_X_scaled)\n    report = classification_report(test_y, preds, target_names=['onion', 'weed'], output_dict=True)\n    print(f'Test Results for Sample {i+19} using Combined Shape and Texture Features:\\n{report}')\n```\nIn this part, we load the test data and calculate features for each of the onion and weed patches in each test image. We then use the trained models to predict the class labels of each patch using shape features only, texture features only, and combined shape and texture features. Finally, we report the precision and recall scores per class for each of the test images for each of the three models.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=4, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 49190, 236888, 5715, 236789, 236751, 506, 3393, 573, 912, 858, 236787, 107, 2717, 6719, 107, 236865, 16959, 1594, 1262, 107, 2181, 236779, 1516, 578, 2977, 107, 1708, 858, 528, 2644, 236769, 236770, 236819, 236764, 236743, 236778, 236770, 1473, 107, 140, 24557, 578, 10137, 236778, 236761, 66710, 236769, 236760, 236789, 2701, 498, 878, 21690, 236747, 236787, 236771, 236778, 236753, 10996, 24557, 236761, 5067, 1606, 107, 140, 15104, 578, 10137, 236778, 236761, 66710, 236769, 236760, 236789, 2701, 498, 878, 21690, 236747, 236787, 236771, 236778, 236753, 10996, 15104, 236761, 5067, 963, 10137, 236778, 236761, 2783, 11913, 236779, 72153, 97189, 236768, 107, 140, 57985, 578, 10137, 236778, 236761, 66710, 236769, 236760, 236789, 2701, 498, 878, 21690, 236747, 236787, 236771, 236778, 236753, 10996, 57985, 236761, 5067, 