 68%|██████▊   | 682/1000 [01:41<00:36,  8.62it/s]INFO 09-15 16:13:49 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-364da781164d44398c6fb65d1ce9ebbe-0: prompt: 'Sure, here\'s the next attribute of Allah and its respective story, meaning of tricky words, and reflection prompts for a guided journal:\n\n1. Al-Jabbar (الجبار)\nMeaning: The Compeller (Compeller means someone who has the power to force others to do something)\nStory: A boy was being bullied at school and didn\'t know what to do. He prayed to Allah and said "Al-Jabbar" for help. Suddenly, he felt a sense of bravery and was able to stand up to the bullies. He was grateful to Allah for being the compeller.\n\nExplanation:\n\n* Compeller means someone who has the power to force others to do something.\n\nReflections:\n\n* What are some ways you can find courage and strength in Allah?\n* How does it feel to know that Allah is the compeller?\n* What are some other times you can say "Al-Jabbar" to remind yourself of Allah\'s empowering nature?\n\nI hope you find this helpful for your guided journal project. Let me know if you have any other questions or if there is anything else I can assist you with.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=21, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 49190, 236764, 1590, 236789, 236751, 506, 2148, 9176, 529, 24238, 532, 1061, 15941, 3925, 236764, 6590, 529, 41086, 4171, 236764, 532, 16856, 62571, 573, 496, 28172, 8884, 236787, 108, 236770, 236761, 1429, 236772, 119171, 2230, 568, 125378, 22410, 236768, 107, 146868, 236787, 669, 4152, 5768, 568, 8891, 5768, 2820, 5026, 1015, 815, 506, 2066, 531, 4912, 3496, 5