INFO 09-15 16:13:50 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-4a60cbd390c24e2b942d47cd7fe5f874-0: prompt: "Week 4: The Power of Visualization\n\nTable of Contents:\n\n* Introduction\n* Main Course Content\n\t+ Understanding Visualization\n\t+ The Science Behind Visualization\n\t+ Techniques for Effective Visualization\n\t+ Real-life Examples of Visualization in Action\n* Self-Prompting Questions\n* Application Formula\n\nIntroduction:\nWelcome to week 4 of the course, where we dive deeper into the power of visualization. This week, we'll explore how visualization can help you tap into your creative potential and manifest your deepest desires. You'll learn about the science behind visualization, as well as techniques for effective visualization.\n\nMain Course Content:\n\nUnderstanding Visualization:\nVisualization is a powerful tool that can help you bring your goals and aspirations to life. By visualizing what you want, you create a vivid mental image of what you want to achieve, making it easier to bring your vision to life.\n\nThe Science Behind Visualization:\nVisualization is rooted in the power of the mind. When we visualize, our minds send signals to our bodies that trigger the release of certain hormones and neurotransmitters. These hormones and neurotransmitters help to activate our subconscious mind and bring our desires to life.\n\nTechniques for Effective Visualization:\nThere are many techniques for effective visualization, including guided visualization, visualization journaling, and visualization meditation. Each technique has its own unique benefits and can help you tap into the power of visualization in a way that works best for you.\n\nReal-life Examples of Visualization in Action:\nThere are countless examples of individuals who have used visualization to achieve their goals and aspirations. For instance, Olympic athletes often use visualization techniques to help them perform at their best. Visualization has also been used to help individuals overcome obstacles, such as illness or injury, and to achieve financial success.\n\nSelf-Prompting Questions:\n\n* What are my goals and aspirations?\n* How can visualization help me achieve these goals?\n* What visualization techniques work best for me?\n\nApplication Formula:\n\n1. Set clear, achievable goals and aspirations.\n2. Choose a visualization technique that works best for you.\n3. Visualize your goals and aspirations regularly.\n4. Use positive affirmations to reinforce your visualization.\n5. Take action towards your goals and aspirations.\n6. Celebrate your progress and continue to refine and refine your visualization technique.\n\nBy using visualization, you'll be able to tap into the power of your mind and bring your desires to life. Remember to be patient, persistent, and stay positive. The more you practice visualization, the better you'll become at manifesting your deepest desires.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=24, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 27962, 236743, 236812, 236787, 669, 7338, 529, 154377, 108, 5010, 529, 57070, 236787, 108, 236829, 23051, 107, 236829, 6400, 24435, 16748, 107, 255968, 236862, 40411, 154377, 107, 255968, 236862, 669, 7621, 55815, 154377, 107, 255968, 236862, 57939, 573, 47844, 154377, 107, 255968, 236862, 10170, 236772, 9524, 26935, 529, 154377, 528, 10659, 107, 236829, 15207, 236772, 70517, 522, 23610, 107, 236829, 12518, 32837, 108, 22660, 236787, 107, 16651, 531, 2069, 236743, 236812, 529, 506, 3003, 236764, 1298, 692, 30386, 19276, 1131, 506, 2066, 529, 44751, 236761, 1174, 2069, 236764, 692, 236789, 859, 11327, 1217, 44751, 74