 77%|███████▋  | 766/1000 [01:50<00:30,  7.57it/s]INFO 09-15 16:13:58 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-96e3cdcc35ec4a1f9c9956af0c54c98f-0: prompt: 'Write a detailed status report and items raised to think about or do with speaker from this \n transcript:\nAnila - looking for bigger things in 2023\n\nAnila mentioned “franchise” as another audience in the context of nurture and something “we’ll need to discuss”\nAnila – want to align leads from monthly newsletter to closes but Gina clarified that these are only going to long-term nurtures and that they’re trying to track who re-engages\n\nAnila – added a partner page to the main Quickbooks site and need to drive traffic to that also\n\nAlso – looking to build a more robust partner directory and need to drive traffic to that\n\nAnila mentioned someone on the team (?) was working on messaging – is there an updated deck or messaging for ISVs/MSPs that we can request?\n\nAnila – how can we continue the journey with leads from content syndication\n\nGina – says that partners are saying that content syndication leads (partner webinars) are really good and that the contacts are the right people; but the response to outreach has been mixed\n- offered to create sample scripts/guidance and she seemed open\n\nAnila asked if we could do focus groups for ISVs/MSPs to ask about content needs and what they use\n\nAnila – says they use Enlyft which they consider similar/same to Rev (they use it mainly for sales) so weren’t that interested … HS will reach out to Rev to learn whether it’s worth communicating any differences (and what those differences are)\n\nAnila – we’re trying to be out there in computer software and compete; how do we compete … asks: what else could we be doing that we’re not? (We may need to define better what her KPI or success metric is here … what does she mean when says “compete” more effectively?)\n\nAsks: What else do you need from us? \n\nHS suggestion – Anila said that someone on their team is working 