 80%|███████▉  | 795/1000 [01:52<00:19, 10.78it/s]INFO 09-15 16:14:00 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-75f2fdeb707e47dbb5419eadf7a08f7b-0: prompt: 'Sure, here is a comparison of the four camera modules that have been suggested so far:\n\n1. Arducam IMX477: This camera module features a 12.3MP Sony IMX477 image sensor and supports up to 4 lanes of MIPI CSI-2 output. It has a maximum resolution of 4056x3040 and supports up to 120fps at 1080p. This camera is designed for use with the Jetson platform and is not specifically designed for space applications.\n2. OnSemi AR0135: This is a monochrome CMOS image sensor that features 1.2MP resolution and supports global shutter readout. It is designed for use in machine vision and industrial applications and features high sensitivity, low noise, and a small form factor.\n3. OnSemi KAI-2020: This is a CCD image sensor that features 2MP resolution and supports progressive scan readout. It is designed for use in industrial and scientific applications and features high sensitivity, low noise, and a high dynamic range. This sensor also has a large pixel size of 7.4µm, which can be advantageous in low-light conditions.\n4. e2v EV76C570: This is a monochrome CCD image sensor that features 1.3MP resolution and supports interline transfer readout. It is designed for use in scientific and space applications and features high sensitivity, low noise, and radiation tolerance. This sensor also has a large pixel size of 14µm, which can be advantageous in low-light conditions.\n\nIn general, the OnSemi AR0135, OnSemi KAI-2020, and e2v EV76C570 are more suitable for space applications due to their radiation tolerance and other features that are designed for use in extreme conditions. The Arducam IMX477 is a high-quality camera module, but it is not specifically designed for use in space.\n\nThe choice of camera module ultimately depends on the specific requirements of the space mission, including resolution, sensitivity, dynamic range, radiation tolerance, and other factors. Consulting with experts in space engineering and testing is highly recommended to ensure that the camera module is suitable for the specific space application.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=33, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 49190, 236764, 1590, 563, 496, 9960, 529, 506, 2390, 5873, 19505, 600, 735, 1010, 10340, 834, 2793, 236787, 108, 236770, 236761, 1572, 5327, 546, 12607, 236917, 236812, 236832, 236832, 236787, 1174, 5873, 9173, 4065, 496, 236743, 236770, 236778, 236761, 236800, 5153, 28457, 12607, 236917, 236812, 236832, 236832, 2471, 13064, 532, 12765, 872, 531, 236743, 236812, 44077, 529, 29067, 3516, 102379, 236772, 236778, 3938, 236761, 1030, 815, 496, 5783, 9314, 529, 236743, 236812, 236771, 236810, 236825, 236781, 236800, 236771, 236812, 236771, 532, 12765, 872, 531, 236743, 236770, 236778, 236771, 40426, 657, 236743, 236770, 236771, 236828, 236771, 236758, 236761, 1174, 5873, 563, 5402, 573, 1161, 607, 506, 36734, 1588, 5058, 532, 563, 711, 10916, 5402, 573, 2557, 6182, 236761, 107, 236778, 236761, 2154, 88130, 8886, 236771, 236770, 236800, 236810, 236787, 1174, 563, 496, 63550, 116825, 2471, 13064, 600, 4065, 236743, 236770, 236761, 236778, 5153, 9314, 532, 12765, 4185, 48540, 120469, 236761, 1030, 563, 5402, 573, 1161, 528, 5464, 10040, 532, 8459, 6182, 532, 4065, 1494, 17511, 236764, 2708, 9168, 236764, 532, 496, 1944, 1183, 5415, 236761, 107, 236800, 236761, 2154, 88130, 751, 12553, 236772, 236778, 236771, 236778, 236771, 236787, 1174, 563, 496, 85201, 2471, 13064, 600, 4065, 236743, 236778, 5153, 9314, 532, 12765, 2