INFO 09-15 16:14:01 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-7f0b8c1bee154e3bacce7358528a9bca-0: prompt: 'The Winner-Take-All (WTA) learning rule is a unsupervised learning algorithm used to train artificial neural networks. It is based on the idea that only the neuron with the highest activation value (the "winner") will be updated, while the other neurons will not be updated.\n\nThe WTA learning rule can be mathematically represented as:\n\nΔw\\_i = η(x\\_i - w\\_i) if i = argmax(y\\_i) else 0\n\nWhere w\\_i is the weight between the input and the ith neuron, x\\_i is the input to the ith neuron, y\\_i is the output of the ith neuron, and η is the learning rate (a small positive value that determines how fast the network learns).\n\nFor example, imagine that you want to train a neural network to recognize handwritten digits. The network would be presented with many examples of handwritten digits and the WTA learning rule would be used to adjust the weights of the network so that only the neuron with the highest activation value (the "winner") will be updated, while the other neurons will not be updated.\n\nThe WTA learning rule is used in unsupervised learning tasks, where no labeled examples are provided. It is a simple and efficient algorithm but it requires a large amount of data to work properly.\n\nIn summary, the Winner-Take-All (WTA) learning rule is a unsupervised learning algorithm used to train artificial neural networks. It is based on the idea that only the neuron with the highest activation value will be updated. It is a simple and efficient algorithm but it requires a large amount of data to work properly.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=7, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 818, 67316, 236772, 13751, 236772, 3243, 568, 236824, 8121, 236768, 4735, 6157, 563, 496, 124155, 4735, 8417, 1456, 531, 2519, 16477, 22823, 12230, 236761, 1030, 563, 2721, 580, 506, 4317, 600, 1186, 506, 60438, 607, 506, 7310, 12881, 1550, 568, 1437, 623, 52800, 1373, 795, 577, 10448, 236764, 1651, 506, 1032, 30924, 795, 711, 577, 10448, 236761, 108, 818, 176563, 4735, 6157, 740, 577, 96205, 10725, 618, 236787, 108, 238507, 236765, 19165, 236747, 578, 17546, 236769, 236781, 19165, 236747, 753, 515, 19165, 236747, 236768, 768, 858, 578, 2593, 2074, 236769, 236762, 19165, 236747, 236768, 1663, 236743, 236771, 108, 10936, 515, 19165, 236747, 563, 506, 3825, 1534, 506, 2744, 532, 506, 93181, 60438, 236764, 1123, 19165, 236747, 563, 506, 2744, 531, 506, 93181, 60438, 236764, 570, 19165, 236747, 563, 506, 3938, 529, 506, 93181, 60438, 236764, 532, 17546, 563, 506, 4735, 3136, 568, 236746, 1944, 4414, 1550, 600, 23521, 1217, 4592, 506, 3707, 53228, 769, 108, 2542, 2591, 236764, 14011, 600, 611, 1461, 531, 2519, 496, 22823, 3707, 531, 15256, 94788, 26798, 236761, 669, 3707, 1093, 577, 6212, 607, 1551, 8698, 529, 94788, 26798, 532, 506, 176563, 4735, 6157, 1093, 577, 1456, 531, 6253, 506, 18710, 529, 506, 3707, 834, 600, 1186, 506, 60438, 607, 506, 7310, 12881, 1550, 568, 1437, 623, 52800, 1373, 795, 577, 10448, 236764, 1651, 506, 1032, 30924, 795, 711, 577, 10448, 236761, 108, 818, 176563, 4735, 6157, 563, 1456, 528, 124155, 4735, 9395, 236764, 1298, 951, 26777, 8698, 659, 3847, 236761, 1030, 563, 496, 3606, 532, 8143, 8417, 840, 625, 7087, 496, 2455, 2886, 529, 1262, 531, 981, 9668, 236761, 108, 902, 12323, 236764, 506, 67316, 236772, 13751, 236772, 3243, 568, 236824, 8121, 236768, 4735, 6157, 563, 496, 124155, 4735, 8417, 1456, 531, 2519, 16477, 22823, 12230, 236761, 1030, 563, 2721, 580, 506, 4317, 600, 1186, 506, 60438, 607, 506, 7310, 12881, 1550, 795, 5