 82%|████████▎ | 825/1000 [01:56<00:27,  6.32it/s]INFO 09-15 16:14:04 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-f63bec88812f4bc58ca3ee8239ea6517-0: prompt: "Data visualizations are a powerful way to communicate key findings from data analysis and make complex information more accessible and understandable throughout the organization. Here are some tips for using data visualizations to socialize key findings:\n\n1. Choose the right visualization: The choice of visualization should be based on the nature of the data and the story you want to tell. Common types of visualizations include bar charts, line charts, scatter plots, heatmaps, and infographics.\n2. Keep it simple: Data visualizations should be simple and easy to understand. Avoid clutter and unnecessary details, and use clear labeling and formatting to make the information easy to digest.\n3. Use colors and contrast effectively: Colors and contrast can be used to highlight important information and draw attention to key findings. Use contrasting colors for different categories or data points, and use color to highlight important trends or anomalies.\n4. Tell a story: Use data visualizations to tell a story and convey a message. Use titles, subtitles, and annotations to provide context and guide the viewer's attention to the most important insights.\n5. Make it interactive: Interactive visualizations can allow users to explore the data and gain deeper insights. Use interactive features such as tooltips, filters, and animations to make the visualization more engaging and informative.\n6. Share widely: Share data visualizations widely throughout the organization to ensure that key findings are understood and acted upon. Use email, dashboards, and presentations to share the visualizations with different stakeholders, and encourage feedback and discussion.\n\nOverall, using data visualizations to socialize key findings can be a powerful way to ensure that data-driven insights are understood and acted upon throughout the organization. By choosing the right visualizations, keeping it simple, telling a story, and making it interactive, businesses can communicate complex information clearly and intuitively and drive better decision-making.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=9, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 2100, 151289, 659, 496, 8632, 1595, 531, 17730, 2307, 12396, 699, 1262, 3671, 532, 1386, 3996, 1938, 919, 15283, 532, 57181, 5459, 506, 6261, 236761, 5715, 659, 1070, 11221, 573, 1699, 1262, 151289, 531, 157298, 2307, 12396, 236787, 108, 236770, 236761, 23399, 506, 1447, 44751, 236787, 669, 5313, 529, 44751, 1374, 577, 2721, 580, 506, 4135, 529, 506, 1262, 532, 506, 3925, 611, 1461, 531, 3442, 236761, 13752, 4458, 529, 151289, 3204, 3029, 28494, 236764, 1757, 28494, 236764, 11887, 23299, 236764, 5387, 26233, 236764, 532, 176674, 236761, 107, 236778, 236761, 17608, 625, 3606, 236787, 5774, 151289, 1374, 577, 3606, 532, 3735, 531, 3050, 236761, 39874, 65903, 532, 24837, 4889, 236764, 532, 1161, 3582, 50178, 532, 53892, 531, 1386, 506, 1938, 3735, 531, 23219, 236761, 107, 236800, 236761, 6890, 7913, 532, 9530, 11974, 236787, 19870, 532, 9530, 740, 577, 1456, 531, 8357, 2132, 1938, 532, 4988, 5700, 531, 2307, 12396, 236761, 6890, 68570, 7913, 573, 1607, 12669, 653, 1262, 3298, 236764, 532, 1161, 2258, 531, 8357, 2132, 15067, 653, 53768, 236761, 107, 236812, 236761, 32815, 496, 3925, 236787, 6890, 1262, 151289, 531, 3442, 496, 3925, 532, 17308, 496, 3618, 236761, 6890, 19293, 236764, 99429, 236764, 532, 62708, 531, 2847, 4403, 532, 8214, 506, 31457, 236789, 236751, 5700, 531, 506, 1346, 2132, 