INFO 09-15 16:14:11 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-3e360a07bab642519446869c9e013b77-0: prompt: 'The information in the `bluetooth_hid_notes.md` file in the Nintendo Switch Reverse Engineering repository provides a high-level overview of the Bluetooth HID protocol used by the Joy-Con controller to communicate with the Nintendo Switch. This information is used in the implementation of the Joy-Con controller protocol in the joycontrol library.\n\nThe `joycontrol/controller_state.py` file in the joycontrol repository implements a representation of the state of a Joy-Con controller. The information from `bluetooth_hid_notes.md` is used to define the format and content of the HID reports that are sent and received by the Joy-Con controller, and the code in this file uses that information to implement a data structure that represents the state of the controller.\n\nFor example, the information in `bluetooth_hid_notes.md` describes the format of the HID reports that are used to represent button presses and stick movements on the Joy-Con controller. The code in `joycontrol/controller_state.py` uses that information to define a class that represents the state of the controller, including the button presses and stick movements. When a button press or stick movement is detected, the code updates the state of the controller and sends the corresponding HID report to the Nintendo Switch over Bluetooth.\n\nIn summary, the information in `bluetooth_hid_notes.md` is used in the implementation of the Joy-Con controller protocol in `joycontrol/controller_state.py` to define the format and content of the HID reports that are sent and received by the Joy-Con controller, and to implement a representation of the state of the controller.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=39, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [2, 818, 1938, 528, 506, 2165, 131389, 236779, 31334, 236779, 23184, 236761, 4565, 236929, 2129, 528, 506, 30811, 21446, 72536, 12464, 20387, 4728, 496, 1494, 236772, 5909, 21385, 529, 506, 27227, 135707, 16433, 1456, 684, 506, 25473, 236772, 1505, 13372, 531, 17730, 607, 506, 30811, 21446, 236761, 1174, 1938, 563, 1456, 528, 506, 8688, 529, 506, 25473, 236772, 1505, 13372, 16433, 528, 506, 12690, 8607, 9427, 236761, 108, 818, 2165, 3672, 8607, 236786, 12074, 236779, 3255, 236761, 2551, 236929, 2129, 528, 506, 12690, 8607, 20387, 19301, 496, 10065, 529, 506, 1883, 529, 496, 25473, 236772, 1505, 13372, 236761, 669, 1938, 699, 2165, 131389, 236779, 31334, 236779, 23184, 236761, 4565, 236929, 563, 1456, 531, 8540, 506, 6518, 532, 3004, 529, 506, 135707, 7248, 600, 659, 3265, 532, 4461, 684, 506, 25473, 236772, 1505, 13372, 236764, 532, 506, 3393, 528, 672, 2129, 6178, 600, 1938, 531, 4144, 496, 1262, 3904, 600, 9282, 506, 1883, 529, 506, 13372, 236761, 108, 2542, 2591, 236764, 506, 1938, 528, 2165, 131389, 236779, 31334, 236779, 23184, 236761, 4565, 236929, 15517, 506, 6518, 529, 506, 135707, 7248, 600, 659, 1456, 531, 2754, 4309, 63581, 532, 6568, 18560, 580, 506, 25473, 236772, 1505, 13372, 236761, 669, 3393, 528, 2165, 3672, 8607, 236786, 12074, 236779, 3255, 236761, 2551, 236929, 6178, 600, 1938, 531, 8540, 496, 1012, 600, 9282, 506, 1883, 529, 506, 13372, 236764, 2440, 506, 4309, 63581, 532, 6568, 18560, 236761, 3026, 496, 4309, 2686, 653, 6568, 7296, 563, 13207, 236764, 506, 3393, 12496, 506, 1883, 529, 506, 13372, 532, 25017, 506, 7041, 135707, 2072, 531, 506, 30811, 21446, 1024, 27227, 236761, 108, 902, 12323, 236764, 506, 1938, 528, 2165, 131389, 236779, 31334, 236779, 23184, 236761, 4565, 236929, 563, 1456, 528, 506, 8688, 529, 506, 25473, 236772,